window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b071-a4bd60f5d4a52c76.json"]={sha256:"a4bd60f5d4a52c768ba30d872d13a76d5640a855e6259b9e600865f8f29590a5",value:{"id":"b071","title":"鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗","titleEn":"Welding inspection of major steel joints","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從巨型梁柱接頭與箱型柱續接的傳力出發，說明 1994 年 Northridge 地震焊接接頭脆斷的教訓、厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂、焊接程序與銲工資格、焊接順序與收縮、品管與品保停留點、超音波檢測幾何、尺寸目視檢查、缺陷修補與焊道紀錄，並以 Alexander L. Kielland 平台、I-40 Hernando de Soto 橋與舊金山—奧克蘭海灣大橋東段為實例。","summaryEn":"Starting from force transfer in mega beam–column joints and box-column splices, explain the lessons of brittle weld fractures in the 1994 Northridge earthquake, lamellar tearing and hydrogen cold cracking in thick plate, welding procedures and welder qualification, weld sequence and shrinkage, quality-control and quality-assurance hold points, ultrasonic testing geometry, dimensional visual inspection, defect repair and weld records, with the Alexander L. Kielland platform, the I-40 Hernando de Soto Bridge and the San Francisco–Oakland Bay Bridge East Span as examples.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-concrete-steel","subcategoryTitle":"混凝土與鋼構施工技術","subcategoryTitleEn":"Concrete and steel construction technology","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-concrete-steel","learningTags":["structures","st-concrete-steel","connection"],"architectureFamily":"connection","architectureNodes":[["接頭傳力與焊縫分類","Joint force transfer and weld classes"],["鋼材、焊材與焊接程序","Steel, consumables and procedures"],["預熱、順序與收縮控制","Preheat, sequence and shrinkage"],["品管品保停留點","QC and QA hold points"],["超音波與目視檢測","Ultrasonic and visual testing"],["修補與焊接紀錄","Repairs and weld records"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[0,4]],"diagram":{"type":"connection","labels":["接頭傳力與焊縫分類","鋼材、焊材與焊接程序","預熱、順序與收縮控制","品管品保停留點","超音波與目視檢測"],"labelsEn":["Joint force transfer and weld classes","Steel, consumables and procedures","Preheat, sequence and shrinkage","QC and QA hold points","Ultrasonic and visual testing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：超高層巨型箱型柱 800×800 mm、板厚 60 mm，以全滲透焊做現場續接。(1) 受力：柱在風載下承受拉力 15 MN，斷面積 4×(800 − 60)×60 = 177,600 mm²，平均拉應力 15×10⁶/177,600 ≈ 84.5 MPa。(2) 材料：CE ≈ 0.44、板厚 60 mm，教學假設採最低預熱 110°C、層間溫度上限 230°C；以 30 V、300 A、300 mm/min 施焊，熱輸入 1.8 kJ/mm，須落在 WPS 範圍內。(3) 收縮：A_w = 1,300 mm²，每個續接約 4.5 mm，20 個續接約 90 mm，於柱段長度中預留。(4) 檢驗：70° 斜角探頭在 60 mm 板第一跨聲程約 175 mm；400 道焊縫抽驗 40 道、拒收 3 道，拒收率 7.5% 超過 5%，全面補驗其餘 360 道。(5) 若改變一個輸入：抽驗只拒收 1 道（2.5%），可維持 10% 抽驗，但拒收焊縫仍要追溯銲工並修補後複檢。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築。","textEn":"Design exercise: a supertall mega box column 800×800 mm with 60 mm plates is spliced on site with CJP welds. (1) Demand: the column carries 15 MN of wind tension over an area of 4×(800 − 60)×60 = 177,600 mm², a mean tensile stress of 15×10⁶/177,600 ≈ 84.5 MPa. (2) Material: with CE ≈ 0.44 and 60 mm plate, the teaching assumption is a minimum preheat of 110°C and a maximum interpass temperature of 230°C; welding at 30 V, 300 A and 300 mm/min gives a heat input of 1.8 kJ/mm, which must lie within the WPS range. (3) Shrinkage: with A_w = 1,300 mm², each splice shrinks about 4.5 mm and 20 splices about 90 mm, allowed for in segment lengths. (4) Inspection: a 70° angle probe needs a first-leg sound path of about 175 mm in 60 mm plate; sampling 40 of 400 welds finds 3 rejects, a 7.5% rate above 5%, so the remaining 360 are all tested. (5) Changing one input: with only 1 reject (2.5%) the 10% sampling can continue, but the rejected weld is still traced to its welder, repaired and re-tested. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b071-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類」與「Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints\" and \"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b071-v13-01","title":"巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「梁翼板全滲透開槽焊」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Beam-flange CJP groove weld” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"巨型梁柱接頭、桁架節點與箱型柱續接中，彎矩大多以翼板拉壓力偶傳遞，受拉翼板的全滲透開槽焊必須發揮與母材相同的強度；腹板與加勁板的填角焊則主要承受剪力。焊縫的重要性不只取決於尺寸，而取決於失效後果：位於耐震系統塑性區、承受反覆拉力或疲勞的焊縫，會被歸為需求關鍵焊縫，適用更嚴格的韌性、檢驗與紀錄要求。檢驗計畫因此要先把每一道焊縫分類，而不是一律同樣對待。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「梁翼板全滲透開槽焊」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In mega beam–column joints, truss nodes and box-column splices, moment travels mostly as a tension–compression couple in the flanges, and the complete-joint-penetration (CJP) groove weld on the tension flange must develop the full strength of the base metal, while fillet welds on webs and stiffeners mainly carry shear. A weld's importance depends less on its size than on the consequence of its failure: welds in the yielding zones of seismic systems or under repeated tension or fatigue are classed as demand-critical, with stricter toughness, inspection and record requirements. An inspection plan therefore starts by classifying every weld rather than treating all alike. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Beam-flange CJP groove weld” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：翼板力 F = M/(d − t_f)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Flange force F = M/(d − t_f).","failure":"常見誤解：「焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「梁翼板全滲透開槽焊」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Beam-flange CJP groove weld”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-01-k1","title":"巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類","titleEn":"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints","text":"巨型梁柱接頭、桁架節點與箱型柱續接中，彎矩大多以翼板拉壓力偶傳遞，受拉翼板的全滲透開槽焊必須發揮與母材相同的強度；腹板與加勁板的填角焊則主要承受剪力。焊縫的重要性不只取決於尺寸，而取決於失效後果：位於耐震系統塑性區、承受反覆拉力或疲勞的焊縫，會被歸為需求關鍵焊縫，適用更嚴格的韌性、檢驗與紀錄要求。","textEn":"In mega beam–column joints, truss nodes and box-column splices, moment travels mostly as a tension–compression couple in the flanges, and the complete-joint-penetration (CJP) groove weld on the tension flange must develop the full strength of the base metal, while fillet welds on webs and stiffeners mainly carry shear. A weld's importance depends less on its size than on the consequence of its failure: welds in the yielding zones of seismic systems or under repeated tension or fatigue are classed as demand-critical, with stricter toughness, inspection and record requirements.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints\" is correct?","options":["焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。","巨型梁柱接頭、桁架節點與箱型柱續接中，彎矩大多以翼板拉壓力偶傳遞，受拉翼板的全滲透開槽焊必須發揮與母材相同的強度；腹板與加勁板的填角焊則主要承受剪力。","留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside.","In mega beam–column joints, truss nodes and box-column splices, moment travels mostly as a tension–compression couple in the flanges, and the complete-joint-penetration (CJP) groove weld on the tension flange must develop the full strength of the base metal, while fillet welds on webs and stiffeners mainly carry shear.","Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"巨型梁柱接頭、桁架節點與箱型柱續接中，彎矩大多以翼板拉壓力偶傳遞，受拉翼板的全滲透開槽焊必須發揮與母材相同的強度；腹板與加勁板的填角焊則主要承受剪力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In mega beam–column joints, truss nodes and box-column splices, moment travels mostly as a tension–compression couple in the flanges, and the complete-joint-penetration (CJP) groove weld on the tension flange must develop the full strength of the base metal, while fillet welds on webs and stiffeners mainly carry shear. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b071-v13-02","title":"巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類：定量估算","titleEn":"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「梁翼板全滲透開槽焊」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Beam-flange CJP groove weld” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：翼板力 F = M/(d − t_f)。M = 2,000 kN·m、梁深 d = 0.9 m、翼板厚 t_f = 0.03 m：F = 2,000/0.87 ≈ 2,299 kN；翼板 300×30 mm，面積 9,000 mm²，平均應力 σ = 2,299,000/9,000 ≈ 255 MPa，已接近 Q345 或 A572 Gr. 50 鋼材降伏強度的四分之三，焊縫任何缺陷都直接位於高應力區。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Flange force F = M/(d − t_f). With M = 2,000 kN·m, beam depth d = 0.9 m and flange thickness t_f = 0.03 m, F = 2,000/0.87 ≈ 2,299 kN; a 300×30 mm flange of 9,000 mm² carries σ = 2,299,000/9,000 ≈ 255 MPa, about three quarters of the yield strength of a 345 MPa steel, so any weld flaw sits in a highly stressed zone. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在設計圖與施工圖上以符號標出每一道焊縫的類型（全滲透、部分滲透、填角）、受力方向、是否為需求關鍵焊縫與對應的非破壞檢測等級，製成焊縫清冊；檢驗人員以清冊核對現場，確保沒有焊縫被遺漏或降級。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark on design and shop drawings the type of every weld (CJP, partial-penetration, fillet), its stress direction, whether it is demand-critical and its required NDT level, compiled into a weld register; inspectors check the site against the register so no weld is missed or downgraded.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"翼板力 F = M/(d − t_f)。M = 2,000 kN·m、梁深 d = 0.9 m、翼板厚 t_f = 0.03 m：F = 2,000/0.87 ≈ 2,299 kN；翼板 300×30 mm，面積 9,000 mm²，平均應力 σ = 2,299,000/9,000 ≈ 255 MPa，已接近 Q345 或 A572 Gr. 50 鋼材降伏強度的四分之三，焊縫任何缺陷都直接位於高應力區。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Flange force F = M/(d − t_f). With M = 2,000 kN·m, beam depth d = 0.9 m and flange thickness t_f = 0.03 m, F = 2,000/0.87 ≈ 2,299 kN; a 300×30 mm flange of 9,000 mm² carries σ = 2,299,000/9,000 ≈ 255 MPa, about three quarters of the yield strength of a 345 MPa steel, so any weld flaw sits in a highly stressed zone. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints\", which statement holds?","options":["銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。","只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。","翼板力 F = M/(d − t_f)。"],"optionsEn":["An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure.","If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.","Flange force F = M/(d − t_f)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"翼板力 F = M/(d − t_f)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Flange force F = M/(d − t_f). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b071-v13-03","title":"巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「梁翼板全滲透開槽焊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Beam-flange CJP groove weld” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在設計圖與施工圖上以符號標出每一道焊縫的類型（全滲透、部分滲透、填角）、受力方向、是否為需求關鍵焊縫與對應的非破壞檢測等級，製成焊縫清冊；檢驗人員以清冊核對現場，確保沒有焊縫被遺漏或降級。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark on design and shop drawings the type of every weld (CJP, partial-penetration, fillet), its stress direction, whether it is demand-critical and its required NDT level, compiled into a weld register; inspectors check the site against the register so no weld is missed or downgraded. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：結構設計者必須在圖說中明確指定需求關鍵焊縫與各焊縫的檢驗等級，不能留給製造廠判斷；焊縫清冊列為施工圖審查的必要文件，未經結構工程師核定不得開始製造。","observationEn":"Site practice: The structural designer must specify demand-critical welds and the inspection level of every weld on the drawings rather than leave it to the fabricator; the weld register is a required submittal in shop-drawing review, and fabrication may not start before the structural engineer approves it.","failure":"注意干擾：若施工圖把受拉翼板全滲透焊誤標為一般焊縫，只做目視檢查，內部未熔合或夾渣就會留在接頭中，在地震或強風的大拉力下由缺陷處脆性斷裂，裂縫可能貫穿翼板並延伸到柱翼板。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If shop drawings mislabel a tension-flange CJP weld as an ordinary weld inspected only visually, internal lack of fusion or slag stays in the joint and, under large seismic or wind tension, starts a brittle fracture that can run through the flange into the column flange. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在設計圖與施工圖上以符號標出每一道焊縫的類型（全滲透、部分滲透、填角）、受力方向、是否為需求關鍵焊縫與對應的非破壞檢測等級，製成焊縫清冊；檢驗人員以清冊核對現場，確保沒有焊縫被遺漏或降級。","textEn":"Mark on design and shop drawings the type of every weld (CJP, partial-penetration, fillet), its stress direction, whether it is demand-critical and its required NDT level, compiled into a weld register; inspectors check the site against the register so no weld is missed or downgraded.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"結構設計者必須在圖說中明確指定需求關鍵焊縫與各焊縫的檢驗等級，不能留給製造廠判斷；焊縫清冊列為施工圖審查的必要文件，未經結構工程師核定不得開始製造。","textEn":"The structural designer must specify demand-critical welds and the inspection level of every weld on the drawings rather than leave it to the fabricator; the weld register is a required submittal in shop-drawing review, and fabrication may not start before the structural engineer approves it.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints\"?","options":["在設計圖與施工圖上以符號標出每一道焊縫的類型（全滲透、部分滲透、填角）、受力方向、是否為需求關鍵焊縫與對應的非破壞檢測等級，製成焊縫清冊。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Mark on design and shop drawings the type of every weld (CJP, partial-penetration, fillet), its stress direction, whether it is demand-critical and its required NDT level, compiled into a weld register.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在設計圖與施工圖上以符號標出每一道焊縫的類型（全滲透、部分滲透、填角）、受力方向、是否為需求關鍵焊縫與對應的非破壞檢測等級，製成焊縫清冊；檢驗人員以清冊核對現場，確保沒有焊縫被遺漏或降級。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark on design and shop drawings the type of every weld (CJP, partial-penetration, fillet), its stress direction, whether it is demand-critical and its required NDT level, compiled into a weld register; inspectors check the site against the register so no weld is missed or downgraded. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b071-v13-04","title":"巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類：失效診斷","titleEn":"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「梁翼板全滲透開槽焊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Beam-flange CJP groove weld” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若施工圖把受拉翼板全滲透焊誤標為一般焊縫，只做目視檢查，內部未熔合或夾渣就會留在接頭中，在地震或強風的大拉力下由缺陷處脆性斷裂，裂縫可能貫穿翼板並延伸到柱翼板。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If shop drawings mislabel a tension-flange CJP weld as an ordinary weld inspected only visually, internal lack of fusion or slag stays in the joint and, under large seismic or wind tension, starts a brittle fracture that can run through the flange into the column flange. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢驗計畫因此要先把每一道焊縫分類，而不是一律同樣對待。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An inspection plan therefore starts by classifying every weld rather than treating all alike.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若施工圖把受拉翼板全滲透焊誤標為一般焊縫，只做目視檢查，內部未熔合或夾渣就會留在接頭中，在地震或強風的大拉力下由缺陷處脆性斷裂，裂縫可能貫穿翼板並延伸到柱翼板。","textEn":"If shop drawings mislabel a tension-flange CJP weld as an ordinary weld inspected only visually, internal lack of fusion or slag stays in the joint and, under large seismic or wind tension, starts a brittle fracture that can run through the flange into the column flange.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「巨型接頭的傳力與焊縫分類」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Force transfer and weld classification in major joints\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若施工圖把受拉翼板全滲透焊誤標為一般焊縫，只做目視檢查，內部未熔合或夾渣就會留在接頭中，在地震或強風的大拉力下由缺陷處脆性斷裂，裂縫可能貫穿翼板並延伸到柱翼板。","留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If shop drawings mislabel a tension-flange CJP weld as an ordinary weld inspected only visually, internal lack of fusion or slag stays in the joint and, under large seismic or wind tension, starts a brittle fracture that can run through the flange into the column flange.","Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若施工圖把受拉翼板全滲透焊誤標為一般焊縫，只做目視檢查，內部未熔合或夾渣就會留在接頭中，在地震或強風的大拉力下由缺陷處脆性斷裂，裂縫可能貫穿翼板並延伸到柱翼板。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If shop drawings mislabel a tension-flange CJP weld as an ordinary weld inspected only visually, internal lack of fusion or slag stays in the joint and, under large seismic or wind tension, starts a brittle fracture that can run through the flange into the column flange. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b071-v13-05","title":"Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「背墊板與焊接扇形孔」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backing bars and weld access holes” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"1994 年 1 月 17 日規模 6.7 的 Northridge 地震後，工程師在多棟鋼造抗彎矩構架建築中發現梁柱焊接接頭脆性斷裂，SEAOC、ATC 與 CUREE 同年組成 SAC 聯合團隊，在 FEMA 與加州緊急服務辦公室資助下研究至 2000 年。常見問題包括：留在原處的背墊板與未熔合根部形成類似裂縫的缺口，焊材韌性不足，焊接扇形孔幾何造成應力集中，以及檢驗難以看到下翼板根部。之後的規範要求需求關鍵焊縫使用有韌性保證的焊材、移除背墊板並清根補焊或加填角焊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「背墊板與焊接扇形孔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After the magnitude 6.7 Northridge earthquake of 17 January 1994, engineers found brittle fractures in welded beam–column joints of many steel moment-frame buildings; SEAOC, ATC and CUREE formed the SAC Joint Venture that year and, funded by FEMA and the California Office of Emergency Services, studied the problem until 2000. Common issues included backing bars left in place with unfused roots acting as crack-like notches, weld metal of low toughness, stress concentrations at weld access holes, and inspection that could hardly see the root of the bottom flange. Later codes required demand-critical welds with toughness-rated filler metal, backing removal with back-gouging and reweld, or a reinforcing fillet. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Backing bars and weld access holes” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：根部缺口近似邊緣裂縫，K = 1.12σ√(πa)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Treat the root notch as an edge crack, K = 1.12σ√(πa).","failure":"常見誤解：「留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「背墊板與焊接扇形孔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Backing bars and weld access holes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-05-k1","title":"Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓","titleEn":"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake","text":"1994 年 1 月 17 日規模 6.7 的 Northridge 地震後，工程師在多棟鋼造抗彎矩構架建築中發現梁柱焊接接頭脆性斷裂，SEAOC、ATC 與 CUREE 同年組成 SAC 聯合團隊，在 FEMA 與加州緊急服務辦公室資助下研究至 2000 年。常見問題包括：留在原處的背墊板與未熔合根部形成類似裂縫的缺口，焊材韌性不足，焊接扇形孔幾何造成應力集中，以及檢驗難以看到下翼板根部。","textEn":"After the magnitude 6.7 Northridge earthquake of 17 January 1994, engineers found brittle fractures in welded beam–column joints of many steel moment-frame buildings; SEAOC, ATC and CUREE formed the SAC Joint Venture that year and, funded by FEMA and the California Office of Emergency Services, studied the problem until 2000. Common issues included backing bars left in place with unfused roots acting as crack-like notches, weld metal of low toughness, stress concentrations at weld access holes, and inspection that could hardly see the root of the bottom flange.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake\" is correct?","options":["留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。","鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。","1994 年 1 月 17 日規模 6.7 的 Northridge 地震後，工程師在多棟鋼造抗彎矩構架建築中發現梁柱焊接接頭脆性斷裂，SEAOC、ATC 與 CUREE 同年組成 SAC 聯合團隊，在 FEMA 與加州緊急服務辦公室資助下研究至 2000 年。"],"optionsEn":["Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing.","Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.","After the magnitude 6.7 Northridge earthquake of 17 January 1994, engineers found brittle fractures in welded beam–column joints of many steel moment-frame buildings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"1994 年 1 月 17 日規模 6.7 的 Northridge 地震後，工程師在多棟鋼造抗彎矩構架建築中發現梁柱焊接接頭脆性斷裂，SEAOC、ATC 與 CUREE 同年組成 SAC 聯合團隊，在 FEMA 與加州緊急服務辦公室資助下研究至 2000 年。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After the magnitude 6.7 Northridge earthquake of 17 January 1994, engineers found brittle fractures in welded beam–column joints of many steel moment-frame buildings; SEAOC, ATC and CUREE formed the SAC Joint Venture that year and, funded by FEMA and the California Office of Emergency Services, studied the problem until 2000. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b071-v13-06","title":"Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓：定量估算","titleEn":"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「背墊板與焊接扇形孔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backing bars and weld access holes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：根部缺口近似邊緣裂縫，K = 1.12σ√(πa)。翼板應力 σ = 300 MPa：未熔合深 a = 1 mm 時 K ≈ 1.12×300×√(π×0.001) ≈ 18.8 MPa√m；a = 5 mm 時 K ≈ 42.1 MPa√m，已接近低韌性焊材在低溫下的斷裂韌性量級。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Treat the root notch as an edge crack, K = 1.12σ√(πa). With flange stress σ = 300 MPa, an unfused depth of a = 1 mm gives K ≈ 1.12×300×√(π×0.001) ≈ 18.8 MPa√m, while a = 5 mm gives K ≈ 42.1 MPa√m, approaching the fracture toughness of low-toughness weld metal at low temperature. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：需求關鍵焊縫的焊材須有規定溫度下的 Charpy 衝擊韌性證明，背墊板移除後以清根、磁粉檢測確認根部無缺陷再補焊；完成後以超音波檢測全長，特別注意下翼板根部與扇形孔周圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Demand-critical welds need filler metal certified for Charpy impact toughness at specified temperatures; after removing the backing bar, back-gouge, confirm a sound root by magnetic particle testing and reweld, then ultrasonically test the full length with special attention to the bottom-flange root and around the access hole.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"根部缺口近似邊緣裂縫，K = 1.12σ√(πa)。翼板應力 σ = 300 MPa：未熔合深 a = 1 mm 時 K ≈ 1.12×300×√(π×0.001) ≈ 18.8 MPa√m；a = 5 mm 時 K ≈ 42.1 MPa√m，已接近低韌性焊材在低溫下的斷裂韌性量級。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Treat the root notch as an edge crack, K = 1.12σ√(πa). With flange stress σ = 300 MPa, an unfused depth of a = 1 mm gives K ≈ 1.12×300×√(π×0.001) ≈ 18.8 MPa√m, while a = 5 mm gives K ≈ 42.1 MPa√m, approaching the fracture toughness of low-toughness weld metal at low temperature. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake\", which statement holds?","options":["根部缺口近似邊緣裂縫，K = 1.12σ√(πa)。","焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。","射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。"],"optionsEn":["Treat the root notch as an edge crack, K = 1.12σ√(πa).","Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength.","Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld."],"answer":0,"explanation":"根部缺口近似邊緣裂縫，K = 1.12σ√(πa)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Treat the root notch as an edge crack, K = 1.12σ√(πa). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b071-v13-07","title":"Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「背墊板與焊接扇形孔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backing bars and weld access holes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"需求關鍵焊縫的焊材須有規定溫度下的 Charpy 衝擊韌性證明，背墊板移除後以清根、磁粉檢測確認根部無缺陷再補焊；完成後以超音波檢測全長，特別注意下翼板根部與扇形孔周圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Demand-critical welds need filler metal certified for Charpy impact toughness at specified temperatures; after removing the backing bar, back-gouge, confirm a sound root by magnetic particle testing and reweld, then ultrasonically test the full length with special attention to the bottom-flange root and around the access hole. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：耐震抗彎矩接頭的細部（扇形孔形狀、背墊板處理、補強填角焊）要採用經試驗驗證的接頭型式，任何現場變更都須經結構工程師核准；地震後的檢查計畫要預先指定拆除被覆的抽查接頭位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Seismic moment-connection details (access-hole shape, backing treatment, reinforcing fillets) must follow test-qualified connection types, and any field change needs the structural engineer's approval; post-earthquake inspection plans should name in advance which joints will have fireproofing removed for checks.","failure":"注意干擾：Northridge 後檢查發現，許多斷裂接頭從外觀幾乎看不出異常，必須拆除防火被覆與裝修才看得到裂縫；這說明地震後的鋼構檢查若只做目視巡查，會嚴重低估損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Post-Northridge inspections found that many fractured joints looked almost normal from outside and cracks appeared only after fireproofing and finishes were removed, showing that post-earthquake steel inspections relying on walk-through visual checks badly underestimate damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"需求關鍵焊縫的焊材須有規定溫度下的 Charpy 衝擊韌性證明，背墊板移除後以清根、磁粉檢測確認根部無缺陷再補焊；完成後以超音波檢測全長，特別注意下翼板根部與扇形孔周圍。","textEn":"Demand-critical welds need filler metal certified for Charpy impact toughness at specified temperatures; after removing the backing bar, back-gouge, confirm a sound root by magnetic particle testing and reweld, then ultrasonically test the full length with special attention to the bottom-flange root and around the access hole.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"耐震抗彎矩接頭的細部（扇形孔形狀、背墊板處理、補強填角焊）要採用經試驗驗證的接頭型式，任何現場變更都須經結構工程師核准；地震後的檢查計畫要預先指定拆除被覆的抽查接頭位置。","textEn":"Seismic moment-connection details (access-hole shape, backing treatment, reinforcing fillets) must follow test-qualified connection types, and any field change needs the structural engineer's approval; post-earthquake inspection plans should name in advance which joints will have fireproofing removed for checks.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","需求關鍵焊縫的焊材須有規定溫度下的 Charpy 衝擊韌性證明，背墊板移除後以清根、磁粉檢測確認根部無缺陷再補焊。","修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Demand-critical welds need filler metal certified for Charpy impact toughness at specified temperatures.","A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original."],"answer":1,"explanation":"需求關鍵焊縫的焊材須有規定溫度下的 Charpy 衝擊韌性證明，背墊板移除後以清根、磁粉檢測確認根部無缺陷再補焊；完成後以超音波檢測全長，特別注意下翼板根部與扇形孔周圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Demand-critical welds need filler metal certified for Charpy impact toughness at specified temperatures; after removing the backing bar, back-gouge, confirm a sound root by magnetic particle testing and reweld, then ultrasonically test the full length with special attention to the bottom-flange root and around the access hole. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b071-v13-08","title":"Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「背墊板與焊接扇形孔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backing bars and weld access holes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"Northridge 後檢查發現，許多斷裂接頭從外觀幾乎看不出異常，必須拆除防火被覆與裝修才看得到裂縫；這說明地震後的鋼構檢查若只做目視巡查，會嚴重低估損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Post-Northridge inspections found that many fractured joints looked almost normal from outside and cracks appeared only after fireproofing and finishes were removed, showing that post-earthquake steel inspections relying on walk-through visual checks badly underestimate damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：之後的規範要求需求關鍵焊縫使用有韌性保證的焊材、移除背墊板並清根補焊或加填角焊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Later codes required demand-critical welds with toughness-rated filler metal, backing removal with back-gouging and reweld, or a reinforcing fillet.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"Northridge 後檢查發現，許多斷裂接頭從外觀幾乎看不出異常，必須拆除防火被覆與裝修才看得到裂縫；這說明地震後的鋼構檢查若只做目視巡查，會嚴重低估損傷。","textEn":"Post-Northridge inspections found that many fractured joints looked almost normal from outside and cracks appeared only after fireproofing and finishes were removed, showing that post-earthquake steel inspections relying on walk-through visual checks badly underestimate damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Northridge 地震的焊接接頭教訓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lessons of welded joints in the Northridge earthquake\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。","Northridge 後檢查發現，許多斷裂接頭從外觀幾乎看不出異常，必須拆除防火被覆與裝修才看得到裂縫；這說明地震後的鋼構檢查若只做目視巡查，會嚴重低估損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.","Post-Northridge inspections found that many fractured joints looked almost normal from outside and cracks appeared only after fireproofing and finishes were removed, showing that post-earthquake steel inspections relying on walk-through visual checks badly underestimate damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Northridge 後檢查發現，許多斷裂接頭從外觀幾乎看不出異常，必須拆除防火被覆與裝修才看得到裂縫；這說明地震後的鋼構檢查若只做目視巡查，會嚴重低估損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Post-Northridge inspections found that many fractured joints looked almost normal from outside and cracks appeared only after fireproofing and finishes were removed, showing that post-earthquake steel inspections relying on walk-through visual checks badly underestimate damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b071-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂」與「焊接程序與銲工資格」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate\" and \"Welding procedures and welder qualification\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b071-v13-09","title":"厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「厚板 Z 向性能與預熱」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Through-thickness properties and preheat” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"巨型接頭常用 50 mm 以上的厚板，焊縫收縮會在板厚方向拉扯母材；若鋼板內有平行於表面的非金屬夾雜，就可能沿夾雜層狀撕裂。另一種危險是氫致冷裂：焊材或潮濕帶入的氫、硬化的熱影響區與高拘束應力同時存在時，裂縫可能在焊後數小時至數天才出現。對策是選用 Z 向性能保證的鋼板、使用低氫焊材並保持乾燥、依碳當量與板厚預熱並控制層間溫度。Alexander L. Kielland 平台事故調查也在相關板件中發現層狀撕裂與冷裂。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「厚板 Z 向性能與預熱」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Major joints often use plates thicker than 50 mm, and weld shrinkage pulls the base metal through its thickness; non-metallic inclusions lying parallel to the surface can then cause lamellar tearing. Another danger is hydrogen cold cracking: when hydrogen from consumables or moisture, a hardened heat-affected zone and high restraint stress coincide, cracks may appear hours to days after welding. Remedies are plates with guaranteed through-thickness properties, dry low-hydrogen consumables, preheat chosen by carbon equivalent and thickness, and controlled interpass temperature. The Alexander L. Kielland investigation also found lamellar tearing and cold cracks in the plates involved. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Through-thickness properties and preheat” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：碳當量 CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Carbon equivalent CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「厚板 Z 向性能與預熱」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Through-thickness properties and preheat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-09-k1","title":"厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂","titleEn":"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate","text":"巨型接頭常用 50 mm 以上的厚板，焊縫收縮會在板厚方向拉扯母材；若鋼板內有平行於表面的非金屬夾雜，就可能沿夾雜層狀撕裂。另一種危險是氫致冷裂：焊材或潮濕帶入的氫、硬化的熱影響區與高拘束應力同時存在時，裂縫可能在焊後數小時至數天才出現。","textEn":"Major joints often use plates thicker than 50 mm, and weld shrinkage pulls the base metal through its thickness; non-metallic inclusions lying parallel to the surface can then cause lamellar tearing. Another danger is hydrogen cold cracking: when hydrogen from consumables or moisture, a hardened heat-affected zone and high restraint stress coincide, cracks may appear hours to days after welding.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate\" is correct?","options":["巨型接頭常用 50 mm 以上的厚板，焊縫收縮會在板厚方向拉扯母材；若鋼板內有平行於表面的非金屬夾雜，就可能沿夾雜層狀撕裂。","鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。","銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。"],"optionsEn":["Major joints often use plates thicker than 50 mm, and weld shrinkage pulls the base metal through its thickness.","Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.","An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"巨型接頭常用 50 mm 以上的厚板，焊縫收縮會在板厚方向拉扯母材；若鋼板內有平行於表面的非金屬夾雜，就可能沿夾雜層狀撕裂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Major joints often use plates thicker than 50 mm, and weld shrinkage pulls the base metal through its thickness; non-metallic inclusions lying parallel to the surface can then cause lamellar tearing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b071-v13-10","title":"厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂：定量估算","titleEn":"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「厚板 Z 向性能與預熱」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Through-thickness properties and preheat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：碳當量 CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。C 0.16、Mn 1.45、Cr 0.05、Mo 0.02、V 0.05、Ni 0.10、Cu 0.15（%）：CE = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.024 + 0.017 ≈ 0.44。熱輸入 HI = 60·V·I/(1,000·v)，30 V、300 A、行進速度 300 mm/min：HI = 1.8 kJ/mm；碳當量偏高且板厚大時，需提高預熱並把熱輸入控制在焊接程序範圍內。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Carbon equivalent CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15. With C 0.16, Mn 1.45, Cr 0.05, Mo 0.02, V 0.05, Ni 0.10 and Cu 0.15 (%), CE = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.024 + 0.017 ≈ 0.44. Heat input HI = 60·V·I/(1,000·v); at 30 V, 300 A and 300 mm/min travel, HI = 1.8 kJ/mm; a high carbon equivalent in thick plate calls for higher preheat, with heat input held inside the procedure range. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對鋼板出廠證明的化學成分、Z 向斷面收縮率與超音波探傷結果，焊前以超音波掃描接頭附近母材找出分層；焊接時以接觸式溫度計或測溫筆在距焊道規定距離處確認預熱與層間溫度，並記錄電流、電壓與行進速度以計算熱輸入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check mill certificates for chemistry, through-thickness reduction of area and ultrasonic plate testing, and scan the base metal near the joint ultrasonically before welding to find laminations; during welding, confirm preheat and interpass temperature with a contact thermometer or temperature crayon at the specified distance from the joint, and log current, voltage and travel speed to compute heat input.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"碳當量 CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。C 0.16、Mn 1.45、Cr 0.05、Mo 0.02、V 0.05、Ni 0.10、Cu 0.15（%）：CE = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.024 + 0.017 ≈ 0.44。熱輸入 HI = 60·V·I/(1,000·v)，30 V、300 A、行進速度 300 mm/min：HI = 1.8 kJ/mm；碳當量偏高且板厚大時，需提高預熱並把熱輸入控制在焊接程序範圍內。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Carbon equivalent CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15. With C 0.16, Mn 1.45, Cr 0.05, Mo 0.02, V 0.05, Ni 0.10 and Cu 0.15 (%), CE = 0.16 + 0.242 + 0.024 + 0.017 ≈ 0.44. Heat input HI = 60·V·I/(1,000·v); at 30 V, 300 A and 300 mm/min travel, HI = 1.8 kJ/mm; a high carbon equivalent in thick plate calls for higher preheat, with heat input held inside the procedure range. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate\", which statement holds?","options":["只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。","碳當量 CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。","非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。"],"optionsEn":["If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.","Carbon equivalent CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15.","Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"碳當量 CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Carbon equivalent CE = C + Mn/6 + (Cr+Mo+V)/5 + (Ni+Cu)/15. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b071-v13-11","title":"厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「厚板 Z 向性能與預熱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Through-thickness properties and preheat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對鋼板出廠證明的化學成分、Z 向斷面收縮率與超音波探傷結果，焊前以超音波掃描接頭附近母材找出分層；焊接時以接觸式溫度計或測溫筆在距焊道規定距離處確認預熱與層間溫度，並記錄電流、電壓與行進速度以計算熱輸入。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check mill certificates for chemistry, through-thickness reduction of area and ultrasonic plate testing, and scan the base metal near the joint ultrasonically before welding to find laminations; during welding, confirm preheat and interpass temperature with a contact thermometer or temperature crayon at the specified distance from the joint, and log current, voltage and travel speed to compute heat input. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：厚板接頭的焊接程序要明訂最低預熱、最高層間溫度、熱輸入範圍與焊材烘乾保管要求；對淬火回火等高強度鋼，最終目視與非破壞檢測應在焊後規定的等待時間（例如 48 小時）後進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: Thick-plate procedures must state minimum preheat, maximum interpass temperature, heat-input range and consumable drying and storage; for quenched-and-tempered high-strength steels, final visual inspection and NDT should follow a specified waiting time after welding, such as 48 hours.","failure":"注意干擾：在冬季未預熱就焊接厚板，或焊條暴露在潮濕空氣中過久，焊後隔天才在熱影響區出現細微裂縫；若在完工當下就做完非破壞檢測並放行，這些延遲裂縫會被包覆在防火被覆或混凝土內。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Welding thick plate in winter without preheat, or with electrodes left too long in damp air, lets fine cracks appear in the heat-affected zone a day later; if NDT is done immediately and the joint released, these delayed cracks are sealed inside fireproofing or concrete. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對鋼板出廠證明的化學成分、Z 向斷面收縮率與超音波探傷結果，焊前以超音波掃描接頭附近母材找出分層；焊接時以接觸式溫度計或測溫筆在距焊道規定距離處確認預熱與層間溫度，並記錄電流、電壓與行進速度以計算熱輸入。","textEn":"Check mill certificates for chemistry, through-thickness reduction of area and ultrasonic plate testing, and scan the base metal near the joint ultrasonically before welding to find laminations; during welding, confirm preheat and interpass temperature with a contact thermometer or temperature crayon at the specified distance from the joint, and log current, voltage and travel speed to compute heat input.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"厚板接頭的焊接程序要明訂最低預熱、最高層間溫度、熱輸入範圍與焊材烘乾保管要求；對淬火回火等高強度鋼，最終目視與非破壞檢測應在焊後規定的等待時間（例如 48 小時）後進行。","textEn":"Thick-plate procedures must state minimum preheat, maximum interpass temperature, heat-input range and consumable drying and storage; for quenched-and-tempered high-strength steels, final visual inspection and NDT should follow a specified waiting time after welding, such as 48 hours.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。","核對鋼板出廠證明的化學成分、Z 向斷面收縮率與超音波探傷結果，焊前以超音波掃描接頭附近母材找出分層。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value.","Check mill certificates for chemistry, through-thickness reduction of area and ultrasonic plate testing, and scan the base metal near the joint ultrasonically before welding to find laminations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對鋼板出廠證明的化學成分、Z 向斷面收縮率與超音波探傷結果，焊前以超音波掃描接頭附近母材找出分層；焊接時以接觸式溫度計或測溫筆在距焊道規定距離處確認預熱與層間溫度，並記錄電流、電壓與行進速度以計算熱輸入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check mill certificates for chemistry, through-thickness reduction of area and ultrasonic plate testing, and scan the base metal near the joint ultrasonically before welding to find laminations; during welding, confirm preheat and interpass temperature with a contact thermometer or temperature crayon at the specified distance from the joint, and log current, voltage and travel speed to compute heat input. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b071-v13-12","title":"厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「厚板 Z 向性能與預熱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Through-thickness properties and preheat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在冬季未預熱就焊接厚板，或焊條暴露在潮濕空氣中過久，焊後隔天才在熱影響區出現細微裂縫；若在完工當下就做完非破壞檢測並放行，這些延遲裂縫會被包覆在防火被覆或混凝土內。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Welding thick plate in winter without preheat, or with electrodes left too long in damp air, lets fine cracks appear in the heat-affected zone a day later; if NDT is done immediately and the joint released, these delayed cracks are sealed inside fireproofing or concrete. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Alexander L. Kielland 平台事故調查也在相關板件中發現層狀撕裂與冷裂。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Kielland investigation also found lamellar tearing and cold cracks in the plates involved.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在冬季未預熱就焊接厚板，或焊條暴露在潮濕空氣中過久，焊後隔天才在熱影響區出現細微裂縫；若在完工當下就做完非破壞檢測並放行，這些延遲裂縫會被包覆在防火被覆或混凝土內。","textEn":"Welding thick plate in winter without preheat, or with electrodes left too long in damp air, lets fine cracks appear in the heat-affected zone a day later; if NDT is done immediately and the joint released, these delayed cracks are sealed inside fireproofing or concrete.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚板層狀撕裂與氫致冷裂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lamellar tearing and hydrogen cracking in thick plate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["在冬季未預熱就焊接厚板，或焊條暴露在潮濕空氣中過久，焊後隔天才在熱影響區出現細微裂縫。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。"],"optionsEn":["Welding thick plate in winter without preheat, or with electrodes left too long in damp air, lets fine cracks appear in the heat-affected zone a day later.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在冬季未預熱就焊接厚板，或焊條暴露在潮濕空氣中過久，焊後隔天才在熱影響區出現細微裂縫；若在完工當下就做完非破壞檢測並放行，這些延遲裂縫會被包覆在防火被覆或混凝土內。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Welding thick plate in winter without preheat, or with electrodes left too long in damp air, lets fine cracks appear in the heat-affected zone a day later; if NDT is done immediately and the joint released, these delayed cracks are sealed inside fireproofing or concrete. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b071-v13-13","title":"焊接程序與銲工資格：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Welding procedures and welder qualification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「焊接程序規範與程序評定紀錄」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “WPS and PQR” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"焊接程序規範（WPS）規定製程、焊材、接頭形狀、焊接位置、預熱與熱輸入等變數；它必須是規範預審合格的程序，或以程序評定紀錄（PQR）的試板經拉伸、彎曲與衝擊試驗證明可行。改變重要變數（例如焊材類別、熱輸入範圍或預熱）就需要重新評定。銲工則須以同等或更困難的位置與接頭考試合格，並維持資格有效。檢驗員的第一項工作是確認每一道焊縫都有對應的有效程序，且由合格銲工施焊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「焊接程序規範與程序評定紀錄」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A welding procedure specification (WPS) fixes the process, consumable, joint geometry, position, preheat and heat input; it must be prequalified by the code or proven by a procedure qualification record (PQR) whose test plates pass tension, bend and impact tests. Changing an essential variable, such as consumable class, heat-input range or preheat, requires requalification. Welders must pass tests in the same or more difficult positions and joints and keep their qualifications current. The inspector's first task is to confirm that every weld has a valid procedure and is made by a qualified welder. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “WPS and PQR” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：PQR 焊道金屬在 −29°C 要求平均 ≥ 27 J（20 ft·lbf），單一試片不得低於要求值的 2/3 = 18 J。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A PQR weld metal requiring an average of at least 27 J (20 ft·lbf) at −29°C, with no single specimen below two thirds of it, 18 J, gives 34, 29 and 19 J: average (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J and minimum 19 J ≥ 18 J, a pass; a minimum of 17 J fails even with a passing average.","failure":"常見誤解：「銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「焊接程序規範與程序評定紀錄」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “WPS and PQR”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-13-k1","title":"焊接程序與銲工資格","titleEn":"Welding procedures and welder qualification","text":"焊接程序規範（WPS）規定製程、焊材、接頭形狀、焊接位置、預熱與熱輸入等變數；它必須是規範預審合格的程序，或以程序評定紀錄（PQR）的試板經拉伸、彎曲與衝擊試驗證明可行。改變重要變數（例如焊材類別、熱輸入範圍或預熱）就需要重新評定。","textEn":"A welding procedure specification (WPS) fixes the process, consumable, joint geometry, position, preheat and heat input; it must be prequalified by the code or proven by a procedure qualification record (PQR) whose test plates pass tension, bend and impact tests. Changing an essential variable, such as consumable class, heat-input range or preheat, requires requalification.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焊接程序與銲工資格」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Welding procedures and welder qualification\" is correct?","options":["銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。","焊接程序規範（WPS）規定製程、焊材、接頭形狀、焊接位置、預熱與熱輸入等變數。","焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。"],"optionsEn":["An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure.","A welding procedure specification (WPS) fixes the process, consumable, joint geometry, position, preheat and heat input.","Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"焊接程序規範（WPS）規定製程、焊材、接頭形狀、焊接位置、預熱與熱輸入等變數；它必須是規範預審合格的程序，或以程序評定紀錄（PQR）的試板經拉伸、彎曲與衝擊試驗證明可行。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A welding procedure specification (WPS) fixes the process, consumable, joint geometry, position, preheat and heat input; it must be prequalified by the code or proven by a procedure qualification record (PQR) whose test plates pass tension, bend and impact tests. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b071-v13-14","title":"焊接程序與銲工資格：定量估算","titleEn":"Welding procedures and welder qualification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「焊接程序規範與程序評定紀錄」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “WPS and PQR” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：PQR 焊道金屬在 −29°C 要求平均 ≥ 27 J（20 ft·lbf），單一試片不得低於要求值的 2/3 = 18 J。三支試片 34、29、19 J：平均 (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J，最低 19 J ≥ 18 J，合格；若最低為 17 J，即使平均合格仍判不合格。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A PQR weld metal requiring an average of at least 27 J (20 ft·lbf) at −29°C, with no single specimen below two thirds of it, 18 J, gives 34, 29 and 19 J: average (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J and minimum 19 J ≥ 18 J, a pass; a minimum of 17 J fails even with a passing average. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：開工前審查每份 WPS 與其 PQR 試驗報告，核對焊材型號、板厚範圍與位置是否涵蓋實際接頭；現場抽查銲工資格證與識別號碼，並比對焊道上的銲工標記與每日焊接紀錄，確認是同一人。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before work starts, review each WPS against its PQR test reports and confirm that consumable, thickness range and positions cover the actual joints; on site, spot-check welder certificates and ID numbers and compare weld stamps with daily welding logs to confirm the same person made the weld.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"PQR 焊道金屬在 −29°C 要求平均 ≥ 27 J（20 ft·lbf），單一試片不得低於要求值的 2/3 = 18 J。三支試片 34、29、19 J：平均 (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J，最低 19 J ≥ 18 J，合格；若最低為 17 J，即使平均合格仍判不合格。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A PQR weld metal requiring an average of at least 27 J (20 ft·lbf) at −29°C, with no single specimen below two thirds of it, 18 J, gives 34, 29 and 19 J: average (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J and minimum 19 J ≥ 18 J, a pass; a minimum of 17 J fails even with a passing average. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「焊接程序與銲工資格」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Welding procedures and welder qualification\", which statement holds?","options":["射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。","修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。","PQR 焊道金屬在 −29°C 要求平均 ≥ 27 J（20 ft·lbf），單一試片不得低於要求值的 2/3 = 18 J。"],"optionsEn":["Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld.","A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.","A PQR weld metal requiring an average of at least 27 J (20 ft·lbf) at −29°C, with no single specimen below two thirds of it, 18 J, gives 34, 29 and 19 J: average (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J and minimum 19 J ≥ 18 J, a pass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"PQR 焊道金屬在 −29°C 要求平均 ≥ 27 J（20 ft·lbf），單一試片不得低於要求值的 2/3 = 18 J。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A PQR weld metal requiring an average of at least 27 J (20 ft·lbf) at −29°C, with no single specimen below two thirds of it, 18 J, gives 34, 29 and 19 J: average (34 + 29 + 19)/3 ≈ 27.3 J ≥ 27 J and minimum 19 J ≥ 18 J, a pass; a minimum of 17 J fails even with a passing average. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b071-v13-15","title":"焊接程序與銲工資格：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Welding procedures and welder qualification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「焊接程序規範與程序評定紀錄」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “WPS and PQR” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"開工前審查每份 WPS 與其 PQR 試驗報告，核對焊材型號、板厚範圍與位置是否涵蓋實際接頭；現場抽查銲工資格證與識別號碼，並比對焊道上的銲工標記與每日焊接紀錄，確認是同一人。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before work starts, review each WPS against its PQR test reports and confirm that consumable, thickness range and positions cover the actual joints; on site, spot-check welder certificates and ID numbers and compare weld stamps with daily welding logs to confirm the same person made the weld. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每個焊接工作站張貼適用的 WPS 摘要，檢驗員每班至少抽測一次電流、電壓與行進速度；程序任何變更都須重新提送審查，未經核准的變更所做的焊縫一律列為不符合項目。","observationEn":"Site practice: Post the applicable WPS summary at every welding station and have the inspector check current, voltage and travel speed at least once per shift; any procedure change must be resubmitted for review, and welds made under an unapproved change are recorded as nonconformances.","failure":"注意干擾：為了趕工改用較粗焊線或提高電流，熱輸入超出程序範圍，熱影響區韌性下降；若沒有人發現程序已被改變，試驗合格的 PQR 就不再代表實際焊縫的性能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Switching to a larger wire or higher current to save time pushes heat input outside the procedure range and lowers HAZ toughness; if nobody notices the change, the passed PQR no longer represents the actual welds. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"開工前審查每份 WPS 與其 PQR 試驗報告，核對焊材型號、板厚範圍與位置是否涵蓋實際接頭；現場抽查銲工資格證與識別號碼，並比對焊道上的銲工標記與每日焊接紀錄，確認是同一人。","textEn":"Before work starts, review each WPS against its PQR test reports and confirm that consumable, thickness range and positions cover the actual joints; on site, spot-check welder certificates and ID numbers and compare weld stamps with daily welding logs to confirm the same person made the weld.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每個焊接工作站張貼適用的 WPS 摘要，檢驗員每班至少抽測一次電流、電壓與行進速度；程序任何變更都須重新提送審查，未經核准的變更所做的焊縫一律列為不符合項目。","textEn":"Post the applicable WPS summary at every welding station and have the inspector check current, voltage and travel speed at least once per shift; any procedure change must be resubmitted for review, and welds made under an unapproved change are recorded as nonconformances.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「焊接程序與銲工資格」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Welding procedures and welder qualification\"?","options":["開工前審查每份 WPS 與其 PQR 試驗報告，核對焊材型號、板厚範圍與位置是否涵蓋實際接頭。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。"],"optionsEn":["Before work starts, review each WPS against its PQR test reports and confirm that consumable, thickness range and positions cover the actual joints.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside."],"answer":0,"explanation":"開工前審查每份 WPS 與其 PQR 試驗報告，核對焊材型號、板厚範圍與位置是否涵蓋實際接頭；現場抽查銲工資格證與識別號碼，並比對焊道上的銲工標記與每日焊接紀錄，確認是同一人。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before work starts, review each WPS against its PQR test reports and confirm that consumable, thickness range and positions cover the actual joints; on site, spot-check welder certificates and ID numbers and compare weld stamps with daily welding logs to confirm the same person made the weld. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b071-v13-16","title":"焊接程序與銲工資格：失效診斷","titleEn":"Welding procedures and welder qualification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「焊接程序規範與程序評定紀錄」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “WPS and PQR” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為了趕工改用較粗焊線或提高電流，熱輸入超出程序範圍，熱影響區韌性下降；若沒有人發現程序已被改變，試驗合格的 PQR 就不再代表實際焊縫的性能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Switching to a larger wire or higher current to save time pushes heat input outside the procedure range and lowers HAZ toughness; if nobody notices the change, the passed PQR no longer represents the actual welds. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢驗員的第一項工作是確認每一道焊縫都有對應的有效程序，且由合格銲工施焊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The inspector's first task is to confirm that every weld has a valid procedure and is made by a qualified welder.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了趕工改用較粗焊線或提高電流，熱輸入超出程序範圍，熱影響區韌性下降；若沒有人發現程序已被改變，試驗合格的 PQR 就不再代表實際焊縫的性能。","textEn":"Switching to a larger wire or higher current to save time pushes heat input outside the procedure range and lowers HAZ toughness; if nobody notices the change, the passed PQR no longer represents the actual welds.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊接程序與銲工資格」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Welding procedures and welder qualification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","為了趕工改用較粗焊線或提高電流，熱輸入超出程序範圍，熱影響區韌性下降；若沒有人發現程序已被改變，試驗合格的 PQR 就不再代表實際焊縫的性能。","焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Switching to a larger wire or higher current to save time pushes heat input outside the procedure range and lowers HAZ toughness.","Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為了趕工改用較粗焊線或提高電流，熱輸入超出程序範圍，熱影響區韌性下降；若沒有人發現程序已被改變，試驗合格的 PQR 就不再代表實際焊縫的性能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Switching to a larger wire or higher current to save time pushes heat input outside the procedure range and lowers HAZ toughness; if nobody notices the change, the passed PQR no longer represents the actual welds. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b071-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力」與「品管、品保與檢驗停留點」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress\" and \"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b071-v13-17","title":"焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「對稱分段焊接順序」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Balanced weld sequence” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大型全滲透焊冷卻時沿焊道橫向收縮數公釐，若接頭被周圍構件拘束，收縮變成殘餘拉應力，可能造成裂縫或使構件位置偏移。超高層箱型柱的現場續接，每一個接頭的收縮累積起來會影響樓層標高與垂直度；桁架節點多方向焊接時，焊接順序則決定變形方向。因此要以對稱、分段、由拘束大處往拘束小處的順序施焊，並在製造長度中預留收縮補償。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「對稱分段焊接順序」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large CJP welds shrink several millimetres transversely as they cool; if surrounding members restrain the joint, the shrinkage turns into residual tensile stress that can crack the weld or pull members out of position. In supertall box-column field splices the shrinkage of every joint accumulates into floor-level and plumbness errors, and in truss nodes welded from several directions the sequence decides which way the joint distorts. Welds are therefore made symmetrically, in segments, from the most restrained toward the least restrained area, with shrinkage allowances built into fabricated lengths. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Balanced weld sequence” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：對接焊橫向收縮經驗式 S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: An empirical transverse shrinkage for butt welds is S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d.","failure":"常見誤解：「焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「對稱分段焊接順序」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Balanced weld sequence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-17-k1","title":"焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力","titleEn":"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress","text":"大型全滲透焊冷卻時沿焊道橫向收縮數公釐，若接頭被周圍構件拘束，收縮變成殘餘拉應力，可能造成裂縫或使構件位置偏移。超高層箱型柱的現場續接，每一個接頭的收縮累積起來會影響樓層標高與垂直度；桁架節點多方向焊接時，焊接順序則決定變形方向。","textEn":"Large CJP welds shrink several millimetres transversely as they cool; if surrounding members restrain the joint, the shrinkage turns into residual tensile stress that can crack the weld or pull members out of position. In supertall box-column field splices the shrinkage of every joint accumulates into floor-level and plumbness errors, and in truss nodes welded from several directions the sequence decides which way the joint distorts.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress\" is correct?","options":["焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。","只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。","大型全滲透焊冷卻時沿焊道橫向收縮數公釐，若接頭被周圍構件拘束，收縮變成殘餘拉應力，可能造成裂縫或使構件位置偏移。"],"optionsEn":["Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength.","If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.","Large CJP welds shrink several millimetres transversely as they cool."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大型全滲透焊冷卻時沿焊道橫向收縮數公釐，若接頭被周圍構件拘束，收縮變成殘餘拉應力，可能造成裂縫或使構件位置偏移。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large CJP welds shrink several millimetres transversely as they cool; if surrounding members restrain the joint, the shrinkage turns into residual tensile stress that can crack the weld or pull members out of position. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b071-v13-18","title":"焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對稱分段焊接順序」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Balanced weld sequence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：對接焊橫向收縮經驗式 S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d。焊道斷面積 A_w = 1,300 mm²、板厚 t = 60 mm、根部間隙 d = 3 mm：S ≈ 0.2×1,300/60 + 0.05×3 ≈ 4.3 + 0.15 ≈ 4.5 mm。若柱高方向有 20 個續接，累積約 20×4.5 ≈ 90 mm，必須在柱段長度中預留。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: An empirical transverse shrinkage for butt welds is S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d. With weld area A_w = 1,300 mm², plate thickness t = 60 mm and root opening d = 3 mm, S ≈ 0.2×1,300/60 + 0.05×3 ≈ 4.3 + 0.15 ≈ 4.5 mm. Twenty splices up a column add about 20×4.5 ≈ 90 mm, which must be allowed for in segment lengths. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以首件或代表性接頭量測焊前焊後的間隙、長度與垂直度，比較實際收縮與預估值並修正後續補償量；箱型柱續接完成後量測柱頂標高與傾斜，與施工測量控制網比對，偏差超過允許值時停止上層施工並檢討。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure gap, length and plumb before and after welding on a first or representative joint, compare actual shrinkage with the estimate and correct later allowances; after each box-column splice, survey column-top level and tilt against the construction control network, stopping upper work for review if deviations exceed tolerances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"對接焊橫向收縮經驗式 S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d。焊道斷面積 A_w = 1,300 mm²、板厚 t = 60 mm、根部間隙 d = 3 mm：S ≈ 0.2×1,300/60 + 0.05×3 ≈ 4.3 + 0.15 ≈ 4.5 mm。若柱高方向有 20 個續接，累積約 20×4.5 ≈ 90 mm，必須在柱段長度中預留。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"An empirical transverse shrinkage for butt welds is S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d. With weld area A_w = 1,300 mm², plate thickness t = 60 mm and root opening d = 3 mm, S ≈ 0.2×1,300/60 + 0.05×3 ≈ 4.3 + 0.15 ≈ 4.5 mm. Twenty splices up a column add about 20×4.5 ≈ 90 mm, which must be allowed for in segment lengths. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress\", which statement holds?","options":["對接焊橫向收縮經驗式 S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d。","非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。","焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。"],"optionsEn":["An empirical transverse shrinkage for butt welds is S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d.","Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection.","Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對接焊橫向收縮經驗式 S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"An empirical transverse shrinkage for butt welds is S ≈ 0.2·A_w/t + 0.05·d. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b071-v13-19","title":"焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「對稱分段焊接順序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Balanced weld sequence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以首件或代表性接頭量測焊前焊後的間隙、長度與垂直度，比較實際收縮與預估值並修正後續補償量；箱型柱續接完成後量測柱頂標高與傾斜，與施工測量控制網比對，偏差超過允許值時停止上層施工並檢討。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure gap, length and plumb before and after welding on a first or representative joint, compare actual shrinkage with the estimate and correct later allowances; after each box-column splice, survey column-top level and tilt against the construction control network, stopping upper work for review if deviations exceed tolerances. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：製造廠應提交焊接順序計畫，標示每一道焊縫的施焊順序、分段長度與銲工配置（例如對邊兩人同時施焊），並由結構工程師審查；現場不得因方便而改變順序，變更須重新核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: The fabricator should submit a weld-sequence plan showing the order, segment lengths and welder arrangement for every weld (for example two welders working opposite faces at once), reviewed by the structural engineer; the sequence may not be changed on site for convenience without re-approval.","failure":"注意干擾：若四面箱型柱同時由一側焊完再焊另一側，柱段會向先焊的一側傾斜；拘束很高的節點一次焊滿而不分段，冷卻時在焊根或熱影響區產生橫向裂縫，往往要到超音波檢測才發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Welding one face of a four-sided box column completely before the opposite face tilts the segment toward the first side; filling a highly restrained node in one go without segmenting can crack the root or heat-affected zone transversely on cooling, often found only by ultrasonic testing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以首件或代表性接頭量測焊前焊後的間隙、長度與垂直度，比較實際收縮與預估值並修正後續補償量；箱型柱續接完成後量測柱頂標高與傾斜，與施工測量控制網比對，偏差超過允許值時停止上層施工並檢討。","textEn":"Measure gap, length and plumb before and after welding on a first or representative joint, compare actual shrinkage with the estimate and correct later allowances; after each box-column splice, survey column-top level and tilt against the construction control network, stopping upper work for review if deviations exceed tolerances.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"製造廠應提交焊接順序計畫，標示每一道焊縫的施焊順序、分段長度與銲工配置（例如對邊兩人同時施焊），並由結構工程師審查；現場不得因方便而改變順序，變更須重新核准。","textEn":"The fabricator should submit a weld-sequence plan showing the order, segment lengths and welder arrangement for every weld (for example two welders working opposite faces at once), reviewed by the structural engineer; the sequence may not be changed on site for convenience without re-approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以首件或代表性接頭量測焊前焊後的間隙、長度與垂直度，比較實際收縮與預估值並修正後續補償量。","留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure gap, length and plumb before and after welding on a first or representative joint, compare actual shrinkage with the estimate and correct later allowances.","Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以首件或代表性接頭量測焊前焊後的間隙、長度與垂直度，比較實際收縮與預估值並修正後續補償量；箱型柱續接完成後量測柱頂標高與傾斜，與施工測量控制網比對，偏差超過允許值時停止上層施工並檢討。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure gap, length and plumb before and after welding on a first or representative joint, compare actual shrinkage with the estimate and correct later allowances; after each box-column splice, survey column-top level and tilt against the construction control network, stopping upper work for review if deviations exceed tolerances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b071-v13-20","title":"焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對稱分段焊接順序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Balanced weld sequence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若四面箱型柱同時由一側焊完再焊另一側，柱段會向先焊的一側傾斜；拘束很高的節點一次焊滿而不分段，冷卻時在焊根或熱影響區產生橫向裂縫，往往要到超音波檢測才發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Welding one face of a four-sided box column completely before the opposite face tilts the segment toward the first side; filling a highly restrained node in one go without segmenting can crack the root or heat-affected zone transversely on cooling, often found only by ultrasonic testing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此要以對稱、分段、由拘束大處往拘束小處的順序施焊，並在製造長度中預留收縮補償。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Welds are therefore made symmetrically, in segments, from the most restrained toward the least restrained area, with shrinkage allowances built into fabricated lengths.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若四面箱型柱同時由一側焊完再焊另一側，柱段會向先焊的一側傾斜；拘束很高的節點一次焊滿而不分段，冷卻時在焊根或熱影響區產生橫向裂縫，往往要到超音波檢測才發現。","textEn":"Welding one face of a four-sided box column completely before the opposite face tilts the segment toward the first side; filling a highly restrained node in one go without segmenting can crack the root or heat-affected zone transversely on cooling, often found only by ultrasonic testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊接順序、收縮與殘餘應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Weld sequence, shrinkage and residual stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。","若四面箱型柱同時由一側焊完再焊另一側，柱段會向先焊的一側傾斜；拘束很高的節點一次焊滿而不分段，冷卻時在焊根或熱影響區產生橫向裂縫，往往要到超音波檢測才發現。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.","Welding one face of a four-sided box column completely before the opposite face tilts the segment toward the first side."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若四面箱型柱同時由一側焊完再焊另一側，柱段會向先焊的一側傾斜；拘束很高的節點一次焊滿而不分段，冷卻時在焊根或熱影響區產生橫向裂縫，往往要到超音波檢測才發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Welding one face of a four-sided box column completely before the opposite face tilts the segment toward the first side; filling a highly restrained node in one go without segmenting can crack the root or heat-affected zone transversely on cooling, often found only by ultrasonic testing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b071-v13-21","title":"品管、品保與檢驗停留點：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「焊前、焊中與焊後檢查點」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Before, during and after-weld checks” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"焊接品質主要在焊接過程中決定，完工後的非破壞檢測只能抽查結果。製造廠的品管人員負責焊前組立間隙、坡口角度、清潔與預熱，焊中逐層檢查與清根，焊後外觀與尺寸；業主委託的品保人員則獨立觀察與抽驗。2005 年舊金山—奧克蘭海灣大橋東段工程的焊接品質遭前銲工與檢驗員指控後，FHWA 委託民間檢驗單位切取鋼塊做實驗室分析，報告三塊試件的焊道符合或超過規範，這種獨立驗證正是品保的角色。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「焊前、焊中與焊後檢查點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Weld quality is decided mainly during welding; NDT after completion only samples the result. The fabricator's quality-control staff check fit-up gap, bevel angle, cleanliness and preheat before welding, each pass and back-gouging during welding, and appearance and size afterwards, while the owner's quality-assurance staff observe and sample independently. In 2005, after former welders and inspectors alleged poor welding on the San Francisco–Oakland Bay Bridge East Span project, FHWA had private inspectors cut sections for laboratory analysis and reported that welds from three pieces met or exceeded specifications, an example of exactly this kind of independent assurance. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Before, during and after-weld checks” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：某批 400 道全滲透焊，抽驗 10% 即 40 道超音波，發現 3 道拒收：拒收率 3/40 = 7.5%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: In a lot of 400 CJP welds, a 10% sample of 40 is ultrasonically tested and 3 are rejected: a reject rate of 3/40 = 7.5%.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「焊前、焊中與焊後檢查點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Before, during and after-weld checks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-21-k1","title":"品管、品保與檢驗停留點","titleEn":"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points","text":"焊接品質主要在焊接過程中決定，完工後的非破壞檢測只能抽查結果。製造廠的品管人員負責焊前組立間隙、坡口角度、清潔與預熱，焊中逐層檢查與清根，焊後外觀與尺寸；業主委託的品保人員則獨立觀察與抽驗。","textEn":"Weld quality is decided mainly during welding; NDT after completion only samples the result. The fabricator's quality-control staff check fit-up gap, bevel angle, cleanliness and preheat before welding, each pass and back-gouging during welding, and appearance and size afterwards, while the owner's quality-assurance staff observe and sample independently.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「品管、品保與檢驗停留點」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points\" is correct?","options":["焊接品質主要在焊接過程中決定，完工後的非破壞檢測只能抽查結果。","只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。","射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。"],"optionsEn":["Weld quality is decided mainly during welding; NDT after completion only samples the result.","If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.","Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld."],"answer":0,"explanation":"焊接品質主要在焊接過程中決定，完工後的非破壞檢測只能抽查結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Weld quality is decided mainly during welding; NDT after completion only samples the result. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b071-v13-22","title":"品管、品保與檢驗停留點：定量估算","titleEn":"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「焊前、焊中與焊後檢查點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Before, during and after-weld checks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：某批 400 道全滲透焊，抽驗 10% 即 40 道超音波，發現 3 道拒收：拒收率 3/40 = 7.5%。若規格規定拒收率超過 5% 時改為 100% 檢測，其餘 360 道須全部補驗；若只有 1 道拒收（2.5%），可維持抽驗比例。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: In a lot of 400 CJP welds, a 10% sample of 40 is ultrasonically tested and 3 are rejected: a reject rate of 3/40 = 7.5%. If the specification switches to 100% testing above 5%, the remaining 360 welds must all be tested; with only 1 rejection (2.5%) the sampling rate could stay. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以檢驗計畫表列出每類焊縫的觀察項目（組立、預熱、清根、外觀）與頻率，並設置停留點：例如清根後須經檢驗員確認才能繼續、全部檢驗合格前不得塗裝或包覆；每個停留點以簽名與時間記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tabulate in the inspection plan the observation items (fit-up, preheat, back-gouge, appearance) and frequency for each weld class, and set hold points such as inspector release after back-gouging before welding continues, and no painting or encasement before all tests pass; record each hold point with signature and time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"某批 400 道全滲透焊，抽驗 10% 即 40 道超音波，發現 3 道拒收：拒收率 3/40 = 7.5%。若規格規定拒收率超過 5% 時改為 100% 檢測，其餘 360 道須全部補驗；若只有 1 道拒收（2.5%），可維持抽驗比例。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"In a lot of 400 CJP welds, a 10% sample of 40 is ultrasonically tested and 3 are rejected: a reject rate of 3/40 = 7.5%. If the specification switches to 100% testing above 5%, the remaining 360 welds must all be tested; with only 1 rejection (2.5%) the sampling rate could stay. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「品管、品保與檢驗停留點」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points\", which statement holds?","options":["修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。","某批 400 道全滲透焊，抽驗 10% 即 40 道超音波，發現 3 道拒收：拒收率 3/40 = 7.5%。","焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。"],"optionsEn":["A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.","In a lot of 400 CJP welds, a 10% sample of 40 is ultrasonically tested and 3 are rejected: a reject rate of 3/40 = 7.5%.","A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"某批 400 道全滲透焊，抽驗 10% 即 40 道超音波，發現 3 道拒收：拒收率 3/40 = 7.5%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"In a lot of 400 CJP welds, a 10% sample of 40 is ultrasonically tested and 3 are rejected: a reject rate of 3/40 = 7.5%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b071-v13-23","title":"品管、品保與檢驗停留點：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「焊前、焊中與焊後檢查點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Before, during and after-weld checks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以檢驗計畫表列出每類焊縫的觀察項目（組立、預熱、清根、外觀）與頻率，並設置停留點：例如清根後須經檢驗員確認才能繼續、全部檢驗合格前不得塗裝或包覆；每個停留點以簽名與時間記錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tabulate in the inspection plan the observation items (fit-up, preheat, back-gouge, appearance) and frequency for each weld class, and set hold points such as inspector release after back-gouging before welding continues, and no painting or encasement before all tests pass; record each hold point with signature and time. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：品保檢驗員應由業主直接委託並獨立於製造廠，擁有停工權；檢驗計畫明訂抽驗比例與拒收率升級規則，所有拒收焊縫都追溯到銲工與班次，作為擴大檢驗的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Quality-assurance inspectors should be hired directly by the owner, independent of the fabricator and empowered to stop work; the inspection plan fixes sampling rates and escalation rules on reject rates, and every rejected weld is traced to its welder and shift as the basis for expanded testing.","failure":"注意干擾：若品管與品保由同一單位擔任，或品保人員只看報告不到現場，焊工趕工時省略清根或預熱也不會被發現；之後即使超音波抽驗合格，也只代表被抽到的焊縫，而非整批品質。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If one party performs both quality control and quality assurance, or assurance staff read reports without visiting the shop, a hurried welder skipping back-gouging or preheat goes unnoticed; a passing ultrasonic sample then represents only the welds sampled, not the lot. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以檢驗計畫表列出每類焊縫的觀察項目（組立、預熱、清根、外觀）與頻率，並設置停留點：例如清根後須經檢驗員確認才能繼續、全部檢驗合格前不得塗裝或包覆；每個停留點以簽名與時間記錄。","textEn":"Tabulate in the inspection plan the observation items (fit-up, preheat, back-gouge, appearance) and frequency for each weld class, and set hold points such as inspector release after back-gouging before welding continues, and no painting or encasement before all tests pass; record each hold point with signature and time.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"品保檢驗員應由業主直接委託並獨立於製造廠，擁有停工權；檢驗計畫明訂抽驗比例與拒收率升級規則，所有拒收焊縫都追溯到銲工與班次，作為擴大檢驗的依據。","textEn":"Quality-assurance inspectors should be hired directly by the owner, independent of the fabricator and empowered to stop work; the inspection plan fixes sampling rates and escalation rules on reject rates, and every rejected weld is traced to its welder and shift as the basis for expanded testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「品管、品保與檢驗停留點」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。","以檢驗計畫表列出每類焊縫的觀察項目（組立、預熱、清根、外觀）與頻率，並設置停留點：例如清根後須經檢驗員確認才能繼續、全部檢驗合格前不得塗裝或包覆。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.","Tabulate in the inspection plan the observation items (fit-up, preheat, back-gouge, appearance) and frequency for each weld class, and set hold points such as inspector release after back-gouging before welding continues, and no painting or encasement before all tests pass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以檢驗計畫表列出每類焊縫的觀察項目（組立、預熱、清根、外觀）與頻率，並設置停留點：例如清根後須經檢驗員確認才能繼續、全部檢驗合格前不得塗裝或包覆；每個停留點以簽名與時間記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tabulate in the inspection plan the observation items (fit-up, preheat, back-gouge, appearance) and frequency for each weld class, and set hold points such as inspector release after back-gouging before welding continues, and no painting or encasement before all tests pass; record each hold point with signature and time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b071-v13-24","title":"品管、品保與檢驗停留點：失效診斷","titleEn":"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「焊前、焊中與焊後檢查點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Before, during and after-weld checks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若品管與品保由同一單位擔任，或品保人員只看報告不到現場，焊工趕工時省略清根或預熱也不會被發現；之後即使超音波抽驗合格，也只代表被抽到的焊縫，而非整批品質。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If one party performs both quality control and quality assurance, or assurance staff read reports without visiting the shop, a hurried welder skipping back-gouging or preheat goes unnoticed; a passing ultrasonic sample then represents only the welds sampled, not the lot. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：2005 年舊金山—奧克蘭海灣大橋東段工程的焊接品質遭前銲工與檢驗員指控後，FHWA 委託民間檢驗單位切取鋼塊做實驗室分析，報告三塊試件的焊道符合或超過規範，這種獨立驗證正是品保的角色。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In 2005, after former welders and inspectors alleged poor welding on the San Francisco–Oakland Bay Bridge East Span project, FHWA had private inspectors cut sections for laboratory analysis and reported that welds from three pieces met or exceeded specifications, an example of exactly this kind of independent assurance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若品管與品保由同一單位擔任，或品保人員只看報告不到現場，焊工趕工時省略清根或預熱也不會被發現；之後即使超音波抽驗合格，也只代表被抽到的焊縫，而非整批品質。","textEn":"If one party performs both quality control and quality assurance, or assurance staff read reports without visiting the shop, a hurried welder skipping back-gouging or preheat goes unnoticed; a passing ultrasonic sample then represents only the welds sampled, not the lot.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「品管、品保與檢驗停留點」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Quality control, quality assurance and hold points\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若品管與品保由同一單位擔任，或品保人員只看報告不到現場，焊工趕工時省略清根或預熱也不會被發現；之後即使超音波抽驗合格，也只代表被抽到的焊縫，而非整批品質。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。"],"optionsEn":["If one party performs both quality control and quality assurance, or assurance staff read reports without visiting the shop, a hurried welder skipping back-gouging or preheat goes unnoticed.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若品管與品保由同一單位擔任，或品保人員只看報告不到現場，焊工趕工時省略清根或預熱也不會被發現；之後即使超音波抽驗合格，也只代表被抽到的焊縫，而非整批品質。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If one party performs both quality control and quality assurance, or assurance staff read reports without visiting the shop, a hurried welder skipping back-gouging or preheat goes unnoticed; a passing ultrasonic sample then represents only the welds sampled, not the lot. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b071-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「超音波與相位陣列檢測」與「目視與尺寸檢查」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing\" and \"Visual and dimensional inspection\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b071-v13-25","title":"超音波與相位陣列檢測：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「超音波斜角探頭掃描」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Angle-beam ultrasonic scanning” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"厚板全滲透焊與 T 型接頭的內部缺陷主要靠超音波檢測：斜角探頭把聲波以固定折射角送入鋼板，遇到未熔合、夾渣或裂縫就反射回來，由聲程與角度換算缺陷深度與位置，再以參考靈敏度判定是否拒收。相位陣列超音波（PAUT）以多個晶片電子控制聲束角度，一次掃描就得到斷面影像，並可留下可重新檢視的數位紀錄。焊前也要掃描母材找出可能導致層狀撕裂的分層。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「超音波斜角探頭掃描」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Internal flaws in thick-plate CJP welds and T-joints are found mainly by ultrasonic testing: an angle-beam probe sends sound into the plate at a fixed refracted angle, lack of fusion, slag or cracks reflect it back, and sound path and angle locate the flaw's depth and position, judged against reference sensitivity for rejection. Phased-array ultrasonics (PAUT) steer the beam electronically with many elements, producing a cross-sectional image in one scan and a digital record that can be reviewed later. Base metal near the joint is also scanned before welding to find laminations that could lead to lamellar tearing. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Angle-beam ultrasonic scanning” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：斜角探頭 θ = 70°，聲程 S = 60 mm 時缺陷深度 d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm，表面距離 = S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For an angle-beam probe at θ = 70° and a sound path S = 60 mm, flaw depth d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm and surface distance S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「超音波斜角探頭掃描」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Angle-beam ultrasonic scanning”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-25-k1","title":"超音波與相位陣列檢測","titleEn":"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing","text":"厚板全滲透焊與 T 型接頭的內部缺陷主要靠超音波檢測：斜角探頭把聲波以固定折射角送入鋼板，遇到未熔合、夾渣或裂縫就反射回來，由聲程與角度換算缺陷深度與位置，再以參考靈敏度判定是否拒收。相位陣列超音波（PAUT）以多個晶片電子控制聲束角度，一次掃描就得到斷面影像，並可留下可重新檢視的數位紀錄。","textEn":"Internal flaws in thick-plate CJP welds and T-joints are found mainly by ultrasonic testing: an angle-beam probe sends sound into the plate at a fixed refracted angle, lack of fusion, slag or cracks reflect it back, and sound path and angle locate the flaw's depth and position, judged against reference sensitivity for rejection. Phased-array ultrasonics (PAUT) steer the beam electronically with many elements, producing a cross-sectional image in one scan and a digital record that can be reviewed later.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超音波與相位陣列檢測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing\" is correct?","options":["射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。","厚板全滲透焊與 T 型接頭的內部缺陷主要靠超音波檢測：斜角探頭把聲波以固定折射角送入鋼板，遇到未熔合、夾渣或裂縫就反射回來，由聲程與角度換算缺陷深度與位置，再以參考靈敏度判定是否拒收。","非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld.","Internal flaws in thick-plate CJP welds and T-joints are found mainly by ultrasonic testing: an angle-beam probe sends sound into the plate at a fixed refracted angle, lack of fusion, slag or cracks reflect it back, and sound path and angle locate the flaw's depth and position, judged against reference sensitivity for rejection.","Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚板全滲透焊與 T 型接頭的內部缺陷主要靠超音波檢測：斜角探頭把聲波以固定折射角送入鋼板，遇到未熔合、夾渣或裂縫就反射回來，由聲程與角度換算缺陷深度與位置，再以參考靈敏度判定是否拒收。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Internal flaws in thick-plate CJP welds and T-joints are found mainly by ultrasonic testing: an angle-beam probe sends sound into the plate at a fixed refracted angle, lack of fusion, slag or cracks reflect it back, and sound path and angle locate the flaw's depth and position, judged against reference sensitivity for rejection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b071-v13-26","title":"超音波與相位陣列檢測：定量估算","titleEn":"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超音波斜角探頭掃描」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Angle-beam ultrasonic scanning” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：斜角探頭 θ = 70°，聲程 S = 60 mm 時缺陷深度 d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm，表面距離 = S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm。60 mm 厚板第一跨（聲波到底面）的聲程 = t/cosθ = 60/0.342 ≈ 175 mm，掃描範圍須依此規劃。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For an angle-beam probe at θ = 70° and a sound path S = 60 mm, flaw depth d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm and surface distance S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm. In a 60 mm plate the first leg to the back wall needs a sound path of t/cosθ = 60/0.342 ≈ 175 mm, which sets the scan range. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢測前以標準規塊校正時基、折射角與參考靈敏度，並以含人工缺陷的對比試塊確認能偵測規定尺寸；掃描須從兩側、多個角度涵蓋整個焊道與熱影響區，記錄每個指示的位置、長度與評級，並由具資格的檢測員簽署。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before testing, calibrate time base, refracted angle and reference sensitivity on standard blocks and confirm on a mock-up with artificial flaws that the required size can be detected; scan from both sides and at several angles to cover the whole weld and heat-affected zone, record position, length and rating of every indication and have a qualified technician sign.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"斜角探頭 θ = 70°，聲程 S = 60 mm 時缺陷深度 d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm，表面距離 = S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm。60 mm 厚板第一跨（聲波到底面）的聲程 = t/cosθ = 60/0.342 ≈ 175 mm，掃描範圍須依此規劃。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For an angle-beam probe at θ = 70° and a sound path S = 60 mm, flaw depth d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm and surface distance S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm. In a 60 mm plate the first leg to the back wall needs a sound path of t/cosθ = 60/0.342 ≈ 175 mm, which sets the scan range. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超音波與相位陣列檢測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing\", which statement holds?","options":["焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。","留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。","斜角探頭 θ = 70°，聲程 S = 60 mm 時缺陷深度 d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm，表面距離 = S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value.","Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing.","For an angle-beam probe at θ = 70° and a sound path S = 60 mm, flaw depth d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm and surface distance S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"斜角探頭 θ = 70°，聲程 S = 60 mm 時缺陷深度 d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm，表面距離 = S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For an angle-beam probe at θ = 70° and a sound path S = 60 mm, flaw depth d = S·cosθ = 60×0.342 ≈ 20.5 mm and surface distance S·sinθ ≈ 56.4 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b071-v13-27","title":"超音波與相位陣列檢測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超音波斜角探頭掃描」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Angle-beam ultrasonic scanning” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢測前以標準規塊校正時基、折射角與參考靈敏度，並以含人工缺陷的對比試塊確認能偵測規定尺寸；掃描須從兩側、多個角度涵蓋整個焊道與熱影響區，記錄每個指示的位置、長度與評級，並由具資格的檢測員簽署。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before testing, calibrate time base, refracted angle and reference sensitivity on standard blocks and confirm on a mock-up with artificial flaws that the required size can be detected; scan from both sides and at several angles to cover the whole weld and heat-affected zone, record position, length and rating of every indication and have a qualified technician sign. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：檢測程序書要指定探頭角度、掃描路徑、校正試塊與允收標準，相位陣列檢測的原始資料檔須保存並交給業主；檢測員資格（例如 ASNT 或 ISO 9712 二級以上）與檢測時間須記錄在報告中。","observationEn":"Site practice: The procedure must specify probe angles, scan paths, calibration blocks and acceptance criteria, and raw PAUT data files must be kept and delivered to the owner; technician qualification (for example ASNT or ISO 9712 Level II or higher) and test timing go into the report.","failure":"注意干擾：若只從一側以單一角度掃描，平行於聲束的平面型未熔合可能完全不反射而被漏判；耦合劑不足或表面有焊濺物，也會使靈敏度下降，讓應拒收的缺陷看起來可以接受。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Scanning from one side at a single angle can miss a planar lack-of-fusion flaw lying parallel to the beam, which returns no echo; poor couplant or weld spatter on the surface lowers sensitivity so that a rejectable flaw looks acceptable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢測前以標準規塊校正時基、折射角與參考靈敏度，並以含人工缺陷的對比試塊確認能偵測規定尺寸；掃描須從兩側、多個角度涵蓋整個焊道與熱影響區，記錄每個指示的位置、長度與評級，並由具資格的檢測員簽署。","textEn":"Before testing, calibrate time base, refracted angle and reference sensitivity on standard blocks and confirm on a mock-up with artificial flaws that the required size can be detected; scan from both sides and at several angles to cover the whole weld and heat-affected zone, record position, length and rating of every indication and have a qualified technician sign.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"檢測程序書要指定探頭角度、掃描路徑、校正試塊與允收標準，相位陣列檢測的原始資料檔須保存並交給業主；檢測員資格（例如 ASNT 或 ISO 9712 二級以上）與檢測時間須記錄在報告中。","textEn":"The procedure must specify probe angles, scan paths, calibration blocks and acceptance criteria, and raw PAUT data files must be kept and delivered to the owner; technician qualification (for example ASNT or ISO 9712 Level II or higher) and test timing go into the report.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超音波與相位陣列檢測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing\"?","options":["檢測前以標準規塊校正時基、折射角與參考靈敏度，並以含人工缺陷的對比試塊確認能偵測規定尺寸。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。"],"optionsEn":["Before testing, calibrate time base, refracted angle and reference sensitivity on standard blocks and confirm on a mock-up with artificial flaws that the required size can be detected.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"檢測前以標準規塊校正時基、折射角與參考靈敏度，並以含人工缺陷的對比試塊確認能偵測規定尺寸；掃描須從兩側、多個角度涵蓋整個焊道與熱影響區，記錄每個指示的位置、長度與評級，並由具資格的檢測員簽署。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before testing, calibrate time base, refracted angle and reference sensitivity on standard blocks and confirm on a mock-up with artificial flaws that the required size can be detected; scan from both sides and at several angles to cover the whole weld and heat-affected zone, record position, length and rating of every indication and have a qualified technician sign. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b071-v13-28","title":"超音波與相位陣列檢測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超音波斜角探頭掃描」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Angle-beam ultrasonic scanning” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只從一側以單一角度掃描，平行於聲束的平面型未熔合可能完全不反射而被漏判；耦合劑不足或表面有焊濺物，也會使靈敏度下降，讓應拒收的缺陷看起來可以接受。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Scanning from one side at a single angle can miss a planar lack-of-fusion flaw lying parallel to the beam, which returns no echo; poor couplant or weld spatter on the surface lowers sensitivity so that a rejectable flaw looks acceptable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：焊前也要掃描母材找出可能導致層狀撕裂的分層。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Base metal near the joint is also scanned before welding to find laminations that could lead to lamellar tearing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只從一側以單一角度掃描，平行於聲束的平面型未熔合可能完全不反射而被漏判；耦合劑不足或表面有焊濺物，也會使靈敏度下降，讓應拒收的缺陷看起來可以接受。","textEn":"Scanning from one side at a single angle can miss a planar lack-of-fusion flaw lying parallel to the beam, which returns no echo; poor couplant or weld spatter on the surface lowers sensitivity so that a rejectable flaw looks acceptable.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超音波與相位陣列檢測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ultrasonic and phased-array testing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只從一側以單一角度掃描，平行於聲束的平面型未熔合可能完全不反射而被漏判；耦合劑不足或表面有焊濺物，也會使靈敏度下降，讓應拒收的缺陷看起來可以接受。","非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Scanning from one side at a single angle can miss a planar lack-of-fusion flaw lying parallel to the beam, which returns no echo.","Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只從一側以單一角度掃描，平行於聲束的平面型未熔合可能完全不反射而被漏判；耦合劑不足或表面有焊濺物，也會使靈敏度下降，讓應拒收的缺陷看起來可以接受。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Scanning from one side at a single angle can miss a planar lack-of-fusion flaw lying parallel to the beam, which returns no echo; poor couplant or weld spatter on the surface lowers sensitivity so that a rejectable flaw looks acceptable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b071-v13-29","title":"目視與尺寸檢查：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Visual and dimensional inspection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「填角焊腳長量規」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fillet-weld size gauge” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"目視檢查是最基本也最常被輕視的焊接檢驗：焊腳尺寸、喉厚、餘高、咬邊、焊瘤、表面氣孔與弧坑裂縫，都可以用量規、放大鏡與良好照明找出來。巨型接頭中大量的填角焊承受剪力，尺寸不足會直接降低強度；咬邊與焊瘤則在焊趾形成缺口，降低疲勞強度。Kielland 平台的 6 mm 填角焊因焊道輪廓不良而降低疲勞強度，說明非主要受力的附屬焊縫也必須被檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「填角焊腳長量規」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Visual inspection is the most basic and most often underrated weld check: leg size, throat, reinforcement, undercut, overlap, surface porosity and crater cracks can all be found with gauges, a magnifier and good lighting. Major joints contain many fillet welds carrying shear, and undersize directly reduces strength; undercut and overlap notch the weld toe and cut fatigue strength. On the Kielland platform a 6 mm fillet weld with a poor profile had reduced fatigue strength, showing that welds on non-load-bearing attachments must be inspected too. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fillet-weld size gauge” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：填角焊有效喉厚 a = 0.707·s，每 mm 強度 φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Fillet-weld effective throat a = 0.707·s and strength per mm φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a.","failure":"常見誤解：「非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「填角焊腳長量規」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fillet-weld size gauge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-29-k1","title":"目視與尺寸檢查","titleEn":"Visual and dimensional inspection","text":"目視檢查是最基本也最常被輕視的焊接檢驗：焊腳尺寸、喉厚、餘高、咬邊、焊瘤、表面氣孔與弧坑裂縫，都可以用量規、放大鏡與良好照明找出來。巨型接頭中大量的填角焊承受剪力，尺寸不足會直接降低強度；咬邊與焊瘤則在焊趾形成缺口，降低疲勞強度。","textEn":"Visual inspection is the most basic and most often underrated weld check: leg size, throat, reinforcement, undercut, overlap, surface porosity and crater cracks can all be found with gauges, a magnifier and good lighting. Major joints contain many fillet welds carrying shear, and undersize directly reduces strength; undercut and overlap notch the weld toe and cut fatigue strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「目視與尺寸檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual and dimensional inspection\" is correct?","options":["非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。","修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。","目視檢查是最基本也最常被輕視的焊接檢驗：焊腳尺寸、喉厚、餘高、咬邊、焊瘤、表面氣孔與弧坑裂縫，都可以用量規、放大鏡與良好照明找出來。"],"optionsEn":["Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection.","A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.","Visual inspection is the most basic and most often underrated weld check: leg size, throat, reinforcement, undercut, overlap, surface porosity and crater cracks can all be found with gauges, a magnifier and good lighting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"目視檢查是最基本也最常被輕視的焊接檢驗：焊腳尺寸、喉厚、餘高、咬邊、焊瘤、表面氣孔與弧坑裂縫，都可以用量規、放大鏡與良好照明找出來。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Visual inspection is the most basic and most often underrated weld check: leg size, throat, reinforcement, undercut, overlap, surface porosity and crater cracks can all be found with gauges, a magnifier and good lighting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b071-v13-30","title":"目視與尺寸檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual and dimensional inspection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「填角焊腳長量規」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fillet-weld size gauge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：填角焊有效喉厚 a = 0.707·s，每 mm 強度 φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a。F_EXX = 490 MPa：s = 12 mm 時 a = 8.48 mm，φR ≈ 0.75×0.6×490×8.48 ≈ 1,871 N/mm；若實際只有 10 mm，a = 7.07 mm，φR ≈ 1,559 N/mm，強度少約 17%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Fillet-weld effective throat a = 0.707·s and strength per mm φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a. With F_EXX = 490 MPa, a 12 mm weld has a = 8.48 mm and φR ≈ 0.75×0.6×490×8.48 ≈ 1,871 N/mm; an actual 10 mm weld has a = 7.07 mm and φR ≈ 1,559 N/mm, about 17% weaker. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以焊腳量規沿焊道等間距量測尺寸，記錄不足處的長度與位置，並依規範允許的局部不足長度判定；咬邊深度以深度規量測，焊趾輪廓不良處以磁粉檢查是否有裂縫；淬火回火鋼的最終目視檢查應在焊後規定等待時間後進行。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure leg size with a fillet gauge at regular intervals along the weld, recording the length and location of any undersize and judging it against the local undersize length the code allows; measure undercut depth with a depth gauge and check poor toe profiles for cracks by magnetic particle testing; final visual inspection of quenched-and-tempered steel should follow the specified waiting time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"填角焊有效喉厚 a = 0.707·s，每 mm 強度 φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a。F_EXX = 490 MPa：s = 12 mm 時 a = 8.48 mm，φR ≈ 0.75×0.6×490×8.48 ≈ 1,871 N/mm；若實際只有 10 mm，a = 7.07 mm，φR ≈ 1,559 N/mm，強度少約 17%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Fillet-weld effective throat a = 0.707·s and strength per mm φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a. With F_EXX = 490 MPa, a 12 mm weld has a = 8.48 mm and φR ≈ 0.75×0.6×490×8.48 ≈ 1,871 N/mm; an actual 10 mm weld has a = 7.07 mm and φR ≈ 1,559 N/mm, about 17% weaker. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「目視與尺寸檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual and dimensional inspection\", which statement holds?","options":["填角焊有效喉厚 a = 0.707·s，每 mm 強度 φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a。","焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。","鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。"],"optionsEn":["Fillet-weld effective throat a = 0.707·s and strength per mm φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a.","A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside.","Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control."],"answer":0,"explanation":"填角焊有效喉厚 a = 0.707·s，每 mm 強度 φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Fillet-weld effective throat a = 0.707·s and strength per mm φR = 0.75×0.6×F_EXX×a. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b071-v13-31","title":"目視與尺寸檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual and dimensional inspection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「填角焊腳長量規」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fillet-weld size gauge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以焊腳量規沿焊道等間距量測尺寸，記錄不足處的長度與位置，並依規範允許的局部不足長度判定；咬邊深度以深度規量測，焊趾輪廓不良處以磁粉檢查是否有裂縫；淬火回火鋼的最終目視檢查應在焊後規定等待時間後進行。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure leg size with a fillet gauge at regular intervals along the weld, recording the length and location of any undersize and judging it against the local undersize length the code allows; measure undercut depth with a depth gauge and check poor toe profiles for cracks by magnetic particle testing; final visual inspection of quenched-and-tempered steel should follow the specified waiting time. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：焊縫清冊要納入所有附屬件的焊縫，特別是焊在受拉或疲勞構件上的吊耳、托架與感測器底座；臨時吊耳拆除後要磨平並以磁粉檢查，紀錄位置供日後檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: The weld register must include every attachment weld, especially lugs, brackets and sensor mounts welded to tension or fatigue members; temporary lifting lugs must be ground flush after removal and checked by magnetic particle testing, with their locations recorded for future inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：附屬板件的填角焊常被視為「不重要」而不檢查，但它在受拉主構件上形成疲勞細節；Kielland 平台的斜撐裂縫被認為可追溯到 1976 年施工時的不良焊接，1980 年 3 月 27 日平台傾覆，212 人中 123 人罹難。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fillet welds on attachments are often dismissed as unimportant and left uninspected, yet they create fatigue details on main tension members; the crack in the Kielland platform's brace was traced to poor welding probably dating from construction in 1976, and on 27 March 1980 the platform capsized, killing 123 of the 212 people aboard. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以焊腳量規沿焊道等間距量測尺寸，記錄不足處的長度與位置，並依規範允許的局部不足長度判定；咬邊深度以深度規量測，焊趾輪廓不良處以磁粉檢查是否有裂縫；淬火回火鋼的最終目視檢查應在焊後規定等待時間後進行。","textEn":"Measure leg size with a fillet gauge at regular intervals along the weld, recording the length and location of any undersize and judging it against the local undersize length the code allows; measure undercut depth with a depth gauge and check poor toe profiles for cracks by magnetic particle testing; final visual inspection of quenched-and-tempered steel should follow the specified waiting time.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"焊縫清冊要納入所有附屬件的焊縫，特別是焊在受拉或疲勞構件上的吊耳、托架與感測器底座；臨時吊耳拆除後要磨平並以磁粉檢查，紀錄位置供日後檢查。","textEn":"The weld register must include every attachment weld, especially lugs, brackets and sensor mounts welded to tension or fatigue members; temporary lifting lugs must be ground flush after removal and checked by magnetic particle testing, with their locations recorded for future inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「目視與尺寸檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual and dimensional inspection\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以焊腳量規沿焊道等間距量測尺寸，記錄不足處的長度與位置，並依規範允許的局部不足長度判定。","焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Measure leg size with a fillet gauge at regular intervals along the weld, recording the length and location of any undersize and judging it against the local undersize length the code allows.","Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以焊腳量規沿焊道等間距量測尺寸，記錄不足處的長度與位置，並依規範允許的局部不足長度判定；咬邊深度以深度規量測，焊趾輪廓不良處以磁粉檢查是否有裂縫；淬火回火鋼的最終目視檢查應在焊後規定等待時間後進行。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure leg size with a fillet gauge at regular intervals along the weld, recording the length and location of any undersize and judging it against the local undersize length the code allows; measure undercut depth with a depth gauge and check poor toe profiles for cracks by magnetic particle testing; final visual inspection of quenched-and-tempered steel should follow the specified waiting time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b071-v13-32","title":"目視與尺寸檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual and dimensional inspection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「填角焊腳長量規」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fillet-weld size gauge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"附屬板件的填角焊常被視為「不重要」而不檢查，但它在受拉主構件上形成疲勞細節；Kielland 平台的斜撐裂縫被認為可追溯到 1976 年施工時的不良焊接，1980 年 3 月 27 日平台傾覆，212 人中 123 人罹難。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fillet welds on attachments are often dismissed as unimportant and left uninspected, yet they create fatigue details on main tension members; the crack in the Kielland platform's brace was traced to poor welding probably dating from construction in 1976, and on 27 March 1980 the platform capsized, killing 123 of the 212 people aboard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Kielland 平台的 6 mm 填角焊因焊道輪廓不良而降低疲勞強度，說明非主要受力的附屬焊縫也必須被檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: On the Kielland platform a 6 mm fillet weld with a poor profile had reduced fatigue strength, showing that welds on non-load-bearing attachments must be inspected too.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「非受力的附屬焊縫品質不重要，不需要檢查。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Welds on non-load-bearing attachments do not matter and need no inspection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"附屬板件的填角焊常被視為「不重要」而不檢查，但它在受拉主構件上形成疲勞細節；Kielland 平台的斜撐裂縫被認為可追溯到 1976 年施工時的不良焊接，1980 年 3 月 27 日平台傾覆，212 人中 123 人罹難。","textEn":"Fillet welds on attachments are often dismissed as unimportant and left uninspected, yet they create fatigue details on main tension members; the crack in the Kielland platform's brace was traced to poor welding probably dating from construction in 1976, and on 27 March 1980 the platform capsized, killing 123 of the 212 people aboard.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「目視與尺寸檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual and dimensional inspection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。","附屬板件的填角焊常被視為「不重要」而不檢查，但它在受拉主構件上形成疲勞細節。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.","Fillet welds on attachments are often dismissed as unimportant and left uninspected, yet they create fatigue details on main tension members."],"answer":2,"explanation":"附屬板件的填角焊常被視為「不重要」而不檢查，但它在受拉主構件上形成疲勞細節；Kielland 平台的斜撐裂縫被認為可追溯到 1976 年施工時的不良焊接，1980 年 3 月 27 日平台傾覆，212 人中 123 人罹難。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fillet welds on attachments are often dismissed as unimportant and left uninspected, yet they create fatigue details on main tension members; the crack in the Kielland platform's brace was traced to poor welding probably dating from construction in 1976, and on 27 March 1980 the platform capsized, killing 123 of the 212 people aboard. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b071-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「缺陷修補與重新檢驗」與「焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Defect repair and re-inspection\" and \"Weld records, traceability and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b071-v13-33","title":"缺陷修補與重新檢驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Defect repair and re-inspection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「刨除修補與複檢」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gouge-out repair and re-test” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"被拒收的焊縫要以碳弧刨或研磨把缺陷完全挖除，並以磁粉或滲透檢測確認挖除乾淨，再依核准的修補程序重新預熱與施焊，最後以原檢測方法重新檢驗。修補比原焊接更困難：挖槽窄深、拘束更高，同一位置反覆修補會讓熱影響區反覆受熱而劣化。I-40 Hernando de Soto 橋 2021 年斷裂的調查即指向製造時兩處寬大的焊接修補所引發的氫致裂紋，說明修補焊縫必須與原焊縫一樣受到嚴格控制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「刨除修補與複檢」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A rejected weld is excavated by air-carbon-arc gouging or grinding until the flaw is fully removed, confirmed clean by magnetic particle or penetrant testing, then preheated and rewelded to an approved repair procedure and re-tested by the original method. Repairs are harder than original welds: the excavation is narrow and deep, restraint is higher, and repeated repairs at one spot reheat and degrade the heat-affected zone. The investigation of the 2021 I-40 Hernando de Soto Bridge fracture pointed to hydrogen cracks from two wide weld repairs made during fabrication, showing that repair welds need the same strict control as the originals. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Gouge-out repair and re-test” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：缺陷長 60 mm，兩端各外延 50 mm 挖除，挖槽長 L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm；預熱範圍取各方向至少 max(75 mm, t) 且 t = 60 mm，預熱區長度約 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a 60 mm long flaw excavated 50 mm beyond each end, the gouge is L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm long; with preheat extending at least max(75 mm, t) in every direction and t = 60 mm, the preheated zone is about 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm long.","failure":"常見誤解：「修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「刨除修補與複檢」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Gouge-out repair and re-test”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-33-k1","title":"缺陷修補與重新檢驗","titleEn":"Defect repair and re-inspection","text":"被拒收的焊縫要以碳弧刨或研磨把缺陷完全挖除，並以磁粉或滲透檢測確認挖除乾淨，再依核准的修補程序重新預熱與施焊，最後以原檢測方法重新檢驗。修補比原焊接更困難：挖槽窄深、拘束更高，同一位置反覆修補會讓熱影響區反覆受熱而劣化。","textEn":"A rejected weld is excavated by air-carbon-arc gouging or grinding until the flaw is fully removed, confirmed clean by magnetic particle or penetrant testing, then preheated and rewelded to an approved repair procedure and re-tested by the original method. Repairs are harder than original welds: the excavation is narrow and deep, restraint is higher, and repeated repairs at one spot reheat and degrade the heat-affected zone.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷修補與重新檢驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Defect repair and re-inspection\" is correct?","options":["被拒收的焊縫要以碳弧刨或研磨把缺陷完全挖除，並以磁粉或滲透檢測確認挖除乾淨，再依核准的修補程序重新預熱與施焊，最後以原檢測方法重新檢驗。","修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。","焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。"],"optionsEn":["A rejected weld is excavated by air-carbon-arc gouging or grinding until the flaw is fully removed, confirmed clean by magnetic particle or penetrant testing, then preheated and rewelded to an approved repair procedure and re-tested by the original method.","A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.","Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"被拒收的焊縫要以碳弧刨或研磨把缺陷完全挖除，並以磁粉或滲透檢測確認挖除乾淨，再依核准的修補程序重新預熱與施焊，最後以原檢測方法重新檢驗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A rejected weld is excavated by air-carbon-arc gouging or grinding until the flaw is fully removed, confirmed clean by magnetic particle or penetrant testing, then preheated and rewelded to an approved repair procedure and re-tested by the original method. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b071-v13-34","title":"缺陷修補與重新檢驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Defect repair and re-inspection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「刨除修補與複檢」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gouge-out repair and re-test” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：缺陷長 60 mm，兩端各外延 50 mm 挖除，挖槽長 L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm；預熱範圍取各方向至少 max(75 mm, t) 且 t = 60 mm，預熱區長度約 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm。若同一接頭抽驗 40 道中有 3 道需修補，修補率 7.5%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a 60 mm long flaw excavated 50 mm beyond each end, the gouge is L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm long; with preheat extending at least max(75 mm, t) in every direction and t = 60 mm, the preheated zone is about 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm long. If 3 of 40 sampled welds in a joint need repair, the repair rate is 7.5%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每一處修補都要有修補單：缺陷位置與類型、挖除深度、清除確認方法、修補程序、銲工、預熱紀錄與複檢結果；同一位置第二次以上的修補須經結構工程師核准，並考慮以硬度或韌性試驗確認熱影響區未劣化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Every repair needs a repair record: flaw location and type, excavation depth, method of confirming removal, repair procedure, welder, preheat record and re-test result; a second or further repair at one location should require the structural engineer's approval, with hardness or toughness checks considered to confirm the heat-affected zone has not degraded.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"缺陷長 60 mm，兩端各外延 50 mm 挖除，挖槽長 L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm；預熱範圍取各方向至少 max(75 mm, t) 且 t = 60 mm，預熱區長度約 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm。若同一接頭抽驗 40 道中有 3 道需修補，修補率 7.5%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a 60 mm long flaw excavated 50 mm beyond each end, the gouge is L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm long; with preheat extending at least max(75 mm, t) in every direction and t = 60 mm, the preheated zone is about 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm long. If 3 of 40 sampled welds in a joint need repair, the repair rate is 7.5%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「缺陷修補與重新檢驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Defect repair and re-inspection\", which statement holds?","options":["留下焊接背墊板可以增加接頭強度，因此不需要移除。","缺陷長 60 mm，兩端各外延 50 mm 挖除，挖槽長 L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm。","銲工經驗豐富就可以不按焊接程序施焊。"],"optionsEn":["Leaving the weld backing bar in place adds strength, so it never needs removing.","For a 60 mm long flaw excavated 50 mm beyond each end, the gouge is L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm long.","An experienced welder does not need to follow the welding procedure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷長 60 mm，兩端各外延 50 mm 挖除，挖槽長 L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm；預熱範圍取各方向至少 max(75 mm, t) 且 t = 60 mm，預熱區長度約 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a 60 mm long flaw excavated 50 mm beyond each end, the gouge is L = 60 + 2×50 = 160 mm long; with preheat extending at least max(75 mm, t) in every direction and t = 60 mm, the preheated zone is about 160 + 2×75 = 310 mm long. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b071-v13-35","title":"缺陷修補與重新檢驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Defect repair and re-inspection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「刨除修補與複檢」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gouge-out repair and re-test” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每一處修補都要有修補單：缺陷位置與類型、挖除深度、清除確認方法、修補程序、銲工、預熱紀錄與複檢結果；同一位置第二次以上的修補須經結構工程師核准，並考慮以硬度或韌性試驗確認熱影響區未劣化。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Every repair needs a repair record: flaw location and type, excavation depth, method of confirming removal, repair procedure, welder, preheat record and re-test result; a second or further repair at one location should require the structural engineer's approval, with hardness or toughness checks considered to confirm the heat-affected zone has not degraded. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：修補程序要與原焊接程序一樣事先送審，修補後的非破壞檢測不得低於原檢測等級；修補紀錄與位置必須永久保存並標在竣工焊道圖上，作為日後營運檢查的重點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Repair procedures must be submitted for approval in advance like the original WPS, post-repair NDT must be at least as stringent as the original test, and repair records and locations must be kept permanently and marked on the as-built weld map as priority points for in-service inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：修補時未完全挖除裂縫末端，或為了快速完成而省略預熱，新焊道下方留下氫致裂紋；這類裂縫可能多年後才在使用應力下成長並造成斷裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Leaving the tip of a crack unexcavated, or skipping preheat to finish quickly, leaves hydrogen cracks beneath the new weld that may grow under service stress and fracture years later. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每一處修補都要有修補單：缺陷位置與類型、挖除深度、清除確認方法、修補程序、銲工、預熱紀錄與複檢結果；同一位置第二次以上的修補須經結構工程師核准，並考慮以硬度或韌性試驗確認熱影響區未劣化。","textEn":"Every repair needs a repair record: flaw location and type, excavation depth, method of confirming removal, repair procedure, welder, preheat record and re-test result; a second or further repair at one location should require the structural engineer's approval, with hardness or toughness checks considered to confirm the heat-affected zone has not degraded.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"修補程序要與原焊接程序一樣事先送審，修補後的非破壞檢測不得低於原檢測等級；修補紀錄與位置必須永久保存並標在竣工焊道圖上，作為日後營運檢查的重點。","textEn":"Repair procedures must be submitted for approval in advance like the original WPS, post-repair NDT must be at least as stringent as the original test, and repair records and locations must be kept permanently and marked on the as-built weld map as priority points for in-service inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「缺陷修補與重新檢驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Defect repair and re-inspection\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要完工後的超音波抽驗合格，焊接過程的檢查就可以省略。","每一處修補都要有修補單：缺陷位置與類型、挖除深度、清除確認方法、修補程序、銲工、預熱紀錄與複檢結果。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If post-weld ultrasonic sampling passes, in-process inspection can be skipped.","Every repair needs a repair record: flaw location and type, excavation depth, method of confirming removal, repair procedure, welder, preheat record and re-test result."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每一處修補都要有修補單：缺陷位置與類型、挖除深度、清除確認方法、修補程序、銲工、預熱紀錄與複檢結果；同一位置第二次以上的修補須經結構工程師核准，並考慮以硬度或韌性試驗確認熱影響區未劣化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Every repair needs a repair record: flaw location and type, excavation depth, method of confirming removal, repair procedure, welder, preheat record and re-test result; a second or further repair at one location should require the structural engineer's approval, with hardness or toughness checks considered to confirm the heat-affected zone has not degraded. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b071-v13-36","title":"缺陷修補與重新檢驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Defect repair and re-inspection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「刨除修補與複檢」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gouge-out repair and re-test” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"修補時未完全挖除裂縫末端，或為了快速完成而省略預熱，新焊道下方留下氫致裂紋；這類裂縫可能多年後才在使用應力下成長並造成斷裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Leaving the tip of a crack unexcavated, or skipping preheat to finish quickly, leaves hydrogen cracks beneath the new weld that may grow under service stress and fracture years later. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：I-40 Hernando de Soto 橋 2021 年斷裂的調查即指向製造時兩處寬大的焊接修補所引發的氫致裂紋，說明修補焊縫必須與原焊縫一樣受到嚴格控制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The investigation of the 2021 I-40 Hernando de Soto Bridge fracture pointed to hydrogen cracks from two wide weld repairs made during fabrication, showing that repair welds need the same strict control as the originals.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「修補焊縫只是把缺陷補起來，品質要求可以比原焊縫寬鬆。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A repair weld just fills a defect, so it can be held to a looser standard than the original.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"修補時未完全挖除裂縫末端，或為了快速完成而省略預熱，新焊道下方留下氫致裂紋；這類裂縫可能多年後才在使用應力下成長並造成斷裂。","textEn":"Leaving the tip of a crack unexcavated, or skipping preheat to finish quickly, leaves hydrogen cracks beneath the new weld that may grow under service stress and fracture years later.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「缺陷修補與重新檢驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Defect repair and re-inspection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["修補時未完全挖除裂縫末端，或為了快速完成而省略預熱，新焊道下方留下氫致裂紋；這類裂縫可能多年後才在使用應力下成長並造成斷裂。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。"],"optionsEn":["Leaving the tip of a crack unexcavated, or skipping preheat to finish quickly, leaves hydrogen cracks beneath the new weld that may grow under service stress and fracture years later.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"修補時未完全挖除裂縫末端，或為了快速完成而省略預熱，新焊道下方留下氫致裂紋；這類裂縫可能多年後才在使用應力下成長並造成斷裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Leaving the tip of a crack unexcavated, or skipping preheat to finish quickly, leaves hydrogen cracks beneath the new weld that may grow under service stress and fracture years later. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b071-v13-37","title":"焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Weld records, traceability and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「焊道地圖與檢驗報告」如何影響鋼構巨型接頭焊接檢驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Weld map and inspection reports” governs force, deformation or durability in “Welding inspection of major steel joints”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每一道重要焊縫都應能追溯到鋼板爐號、焊接程序、銲工、施焊日期、預熱紀錄、非破壞檢測報告與修補履歷。這些紀錄在施工期間用來找出系統性問題，例如某位銲工或某個班次的拒收率偏高；在營運期間則讓檢查人員知道哪些接頭曾經修補、哪些附屬件焊在受拉構件上。Kielland 平台與 I-40 橋的事故都顯示，製造時的焊接缺陷可能在多年後才顯現，因此交接文件要讓下一代工程師找得到這些細節。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「焊道地圖與檢驗報告」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Every important weld should trace back to plate heat number, welding procedure, welder, date, preheat record, NDT reports and repair history. During construction these records expose systematic problems, such as one welder or shift with a high reject rate; in service they tell inspectors which joints were repaired and which attachments are welded to tension members. The Kielland platform and the I-40 bridge both show that fabrication weld defects can surface years later, so handover documents must let the next generation of engineers find these details. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Weld map and inspection reports” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以紀錄比較銲工表現：銲工 A 焊 80 道、拒收 2 道，拒收率 2/80 = 2.5%；銲工 B 焊 60 道、拒收 6 道，拒收率 6/60 = 10%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Records compare welders: welder A made 80 welds with 2 rejected, a 2/80 = 2.5% rate; welder B made 60 with 6 rejected, a 6/60 = 10% rate.","failure":"常見誤解：「焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「焊道地圖與檢驗報告」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Weld map and inspection reports”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-37-k1","title":"焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接","titleEn":"Weld records, traceability and handover","text":"每一道重要焊縫都應能追溯到鋼板爐號、焊接程序、銲工、施焊日期、預熱紀錄、非破壞檢測報告與修補履歷。這些紀錄在施工期間用來找出系統性問題，例如某位銲工或某個班次的拒收率偏高；在營運期間則讓檢查人員知道哪些接頭曾經修補、哪些附屬件焊在受拉構件上。","textEn":"Every important weld should trace back to plate heat number, welding procedure, welder, date, preheat record, NDT reports and repair history. During construction these records expose systematic problems, such as one welder or shift with a high reject rate; in service they tell inspectors which joints were repaired and which attachments are welded to tension members.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Weld records, traceability and handover\" is correct?","options":["焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。","每一道重要焊縫都應能追溯到鋼板爐號、焊接程序、銲工、施焊日期、預熱紀錄、非破壞檢測報告與修補履歷。","焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。"],"optionsEn":["Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value.","Every important weld should trace back to plate heat number, welding procedure, welder, date, preheat record, NDT reports and repair history.","A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每一道重要焊縫都應能追溯到鋼板爐號、焊接程序、銲工、施焊日期、預熱紀錄、非破壞檢測報告與修補履歷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Every important weld should trace back to plate heat number, welding procedure, welder, date, preheat record, NDT reports and repair history. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b071-v13-38","title":"焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Weld records, traceability and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「焊道地圖與檢驗報告」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Weld map and inspection reports” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以紀錄比較銲工表現：銲工 A 焊 80 道、拒收 2 道，拒收率 2/80 = 2.5%；銲工 B 焊 60 道、拒收 6 道，拒收率 6/60 = 10%。B 的拒收率為 A 的 4 倍，應暫停其需求關鍵焊縫作業、重新訓練與考試，並把其已完成焊縫的超音波抽驗提高到 100%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Records compare welders: welder A made 80 welds with 2 rejected, a 2/80 = 2.5% rate; welder B made 60 with 6 rejected, a 6/60 = 10% rate. B's rate is four times A's, so B should be stood down from demand-critical welds, retrained and retested, and B's completed welds raised to 100% ultrasonic testing. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接前隨機抽取數道焊縫，從現場焊道標記追溯到銲工、程序、檢測報告與修補單，確認紀錄鏈完整；並檢查竣工焊道圖是否標示所有修補位置、臨時附件移除處與需求關鍵焊縫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before handover, pick several welds at random and trace each from its site mark to welder, procedure, test reports and repair records to confirm an unbroken chain; check that the as-built weld map shows every repair, every removed temporary attachment and every demand-critical weld.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以紀錄比較銲工表現：銲工 A 焊 80 道、拒收 2 道，拒收率 2/80 = 2.5%；銲工 B 焊 60 道、拒收 6 道，拒收率 6/60 = 10%。B 的拒收率為 A 的 4 倍，應暫停其需求關鍵焊縫作業、重新訓練與考試，並把其已完成焊縫的超音波抽驗提高到 100%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Records compare welders: welder A made 80 welds with 2 rejected, a 2/80 = 2.5% rate; welder B made 60 with 6 rejected, a 6/60 = 10% rate. B's rate is four times A's, so B should be stood down from demand-critical welds, retrained and retested, and B's completed welds raised to 100% ultrasonic testing. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Weld records, traceability and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼板越厚越安全，所以厚板接頭不需要特別的焊接控制。","焊接順序只影響外觀與變形，不會影響接頭強度。","以紀錄比較銲工表現：銲工 A 焊 80 道、拒收 2 道，拒收率 2/80 = 2.5%；銲工 B 焊 60 道、拒收 6 道，拒收率 6/60 = 10%。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker plate is always safer, so thick-plate joints need no special welding control.","Weld sequence affects only appearance and distortion, never joint strength.","Records compare welders: welder A made 80 welds with 2 rejected, a 2/80 = 2.5% rate; welder B made 60 with 6 rejected, a 6/60 = 10% rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以紀錄比較銲工表現：銲工 A 焊 80 道、拒收 2 道，拒收率 2/80 = 2.5%；銲工 B 焊 60 道、拒收 6 道，拒收率 6/60 = 10%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Records compare welders: welder A made 80 welds with 2 rejected, a 2/80 = 2.5% rate; welder B made 60 with 6 rejected, a 6/60 = 10% rate. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b071-v13-39","title":"焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Weld records, traceability and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「焊道地圖與檢驗報告」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Weld map and inspection reports” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接前隨機抽取數道焊縫，從現場焊道標記追溯到銲工、程序、檢測報告與修補單，確認紀錄鏈完整；並檢查竣工焊道圖是否標示所有修補位置、臨時附件移除處與需求關鍵焊縫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before handover, pick several welds at random and trace each from its site mark to welder, procedure, test reports and repair records to confirm an unbroken chain; check that the as-built weld map shows every repair, every removed temporary attachment and every demand-critical weld. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合約應規定焊接紀錄以數位格式交付業主，包含焊道地圖、銲工與程序對照、檢測原始資料與修補履歷；業主的維護手冊要指定需定期檢查的焊縫清單，並由結構工程師依修補與疲勞風險排定優先順序。","observationEn":"Site practice: The contract should require weld records delivered digitally to the owner, including weld maps, welder and procedure cross-references, raw NDT data and repair history; the owner's maintenance manual should list welds for periodic inspection, prioritised by the structural engineer according to repair history and fatigue risk.","failure":"注意干擾：若焊接紀錄只以紙本存放在製造廠，工程結束後隨公司搬遷或結束營業而遺失，業主在數十年後發現裂縫時，無法判斷是單一缺陷還是同批焊縫的共同問題，只能全面檢驗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If weld records stay on paper at the fabricator and are lost when it moves or closes, an owner who finds a crack decades later cannot tell whether it is an isolated flaw or common to a whole batch, and must inspect everything. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接前隨機抽取數道焊縫，從現場焊道標記追溯到銲工、程序、檢測報告與修補單，確認紀錄鏈完整；並檢查竣工焊道圖是否標示所有修補位置、臨時附件移除處與需求關鍵焊縫。","textEn":"Before handover, pick several welds at random and trace each from its site mark to welder, procedure, test reports and repair records to confirm an unbroken chain; check that the as-built weld map shows every repair, every removed temporary attachment and every demand-critical weld.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合約應規定焊接紀錄以數位格式交付業主，包含焊道地圖、銲工與程序對照、檢測原始資料與修補履歷；業主的維護手冊要指定需定期檢查的焊縫清單，並由結構工程師依修補與疲勞風險排定優先順序。","textEn":"The contract should require weld records delivered digitally to the owner, including weld maps, welder and procedure cross-references, raw NDT data and repair history; the owner's maintenance manual should list welds for periodic inspection, prioritised by the structural engineer according to repair history and fatigue risk.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Weld records, traceability and handover\"?","options":["交接前隨機抽取數道焊縫，從現場焊道標記追溯到銲工、程序、檢測報告與修補單，確認紀錄鏈完整；並檢查竣工焊道圖是否標示所有修補位置、臨時附件移除處與需求關鍵焊縫。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","射線檢測一定比超音波更適合檢驗所有厚板焊縫。"],"optionsEn":["Before handover, pick several welds at random and trace each from its site mark to welder, procedure, test reports and repair records to confirm an unbroken chain.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Radiography is always better than ultrasonics for every thick-plate weld."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接前隨機抽取數道焊縫，從現場焊道標記追溯到銲工、程序、檢測報告與修補單，確認紀錄鏈完整；並檢查竣工焊道圖是否標示所有修補位置、臨時附件移除處與需求關鍵焊縫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before handover, pick several welds at random and trace each from its site mark to welder, procedure, test reports and repair records to confirm an unbroken chain; check that the as-built weld map shows every repair, every removed temporary attachment and every demand-critical weld. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b071-v13-40","title":"焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Weld records, traceability and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"prerequisiteIds":["b071-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「焊道地圖與檢驗報告」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Weld map and inspection reports” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若焊接紀錄只以紙本存放在製造廠，工程結束後隨公司搬遷或結束營業而遺失，業主在數十年後發現裂縫時，無法判斷是單一缺陷還是同批焊縫的共同問題，只能全面檢驗。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If weld records stay on paper at the fabricator and are lost when it moves or closes, an owner who finds a crack decades later cannot tell whether it is an isolated flaw or common to a whole batch, and must inspect everything. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：Kielland 平台與 I-40 橋的事故都顯示，製造時的焊接缺陷可能在多年後才顯現，因此交接文件要讓下一代工程師找得到這些細節。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The Kielland platform and the I-40 bridge both show that fabrication weld defects can surface years later, so handover documents must let the next generation of engineers find these details.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焊縫檢驗合格後，焊接紀錄就沒有保存價值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once welds pass inspection, the welding records have no further value.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b071-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若焊接紀錄只以紙本存放在製造廠，工程結束後隨公司搬遷或結束營業而遺失，業主在數十年後發現裂縫時，無法判斷是單一缺陷還是同批焊縫的共同問題，只能全面檢驗。","textEn":"If weld records stay on paper at the fabricator and are lost when it moves or closes, an owner who finds a crack decades later cannot tell whether it is an isolated flaw or common to a whole batch, and must inspect everything.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]},{"id":"b071-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊接紀錄、可追溯性與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Weld records, traceability and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若焊接紀錄只以紙本存放在製造廠，工程結束後隨公司搬遷或結束營業而遺失，業主在數十年後發現裂縫時，無法判斷是單一缺陷還是同批焊縫的共同問題，只能全面檢驗。","焊縫外觀平整光滑，就代表內部品質良好。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If weld records stay on paper at the fabricator and are lost when it moves or closes, an owner who finds a crack decades later cannot tell whether it is an isolated flaw or common to a whole batch, and must inspect everything.","A smooth, even weld surface means the weld is sound inside."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若焊接紀錄只以紙本存放在製造廠，工程結束後隨公司搬遷或結束營業而遺失，業主在數十年後發現裂縫時，無法判斷是單一缺陷還是同批焊縫的共同問題，只能全面檢驗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If weld records stay on paper at the fabricator and are lost when it moves or closes, an owner who finds a crack decades later cannot tell whether it is an isolated flaw or common to a whole batch, and must inspect everything. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-sac-steel-project","v13s-mtc-bay-bridge","v13s-tdot-i40-timeline","v13s-wiki-kielland-platform","v13s-wiki-bay-bridge-east-span"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
